1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Åke Pik=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Tyrgil Pik
2 CONT * Gave some of the years 1300-1310 to Gudhem's monastery with his daughter Margaretha his and his deceased wife Kristina land in Slätohult as well as the brother part, which belonged to his wife's brother Björn Gädda and which he 
2 CONC bought from Knut Ebbason.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22%c3%85ke+pik%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_1873&tab=post#tab '''1873''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1300 without day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Åke Pik announces that when his daughter Margareta entered Gudhem's monastery, he donated to her all his and his late wife Kristina's estate in Slätthult; further that he bought from Knut Ebbasson all the goods in the brother cast
2 CONC le that the issuer's wife's brother Björn Gädda owned and also transferred this to the said daughter. This purchase had taken place so that Björn Gädda senior on behalf of the issuer had paid, Björn mentioned with a piece of green
2 CONC  fabric from Ghent, 5 cattle and 20 marks of money.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003645801906?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000178117766140 '''The issuer seals. SEAL: The seal undamaged, on a strip cut from the letter''']
2 CONT * Extra text: On the reverse: Per predia slætaholt; with newer hand: Åke Pijk.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Källa: PHT 1909, genelogiska anteckningar av K.H.Karlsson
2 CONT * Original:  Or. perg. RA 0101  images
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Peringskiöld: E 46 f. 9r (reg.); Örnhielm: IV pp. 726. Photocopy:  DK
2 CONT * Cf. PHT 1909, pp. 16-22.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Tidigare har uppgetts av Jan Raneke i Svenska medeltidsvapen att Åke Pik och Kristina Giedda (Gäddaätten) hade 5 barn: Margareta, Ebbe Pik, Fjällar, Johan, och Arvid, vilket efter senare forskning har tillbakavisats, och enligt Ka
2 CONC j Janzon kan endast dottern Margareta knytas till Åke med befintliga källor, [4] från år 1300 när Åke Pik nämns som svåger till Björn Gädda (Gäddaätten) i en kungörelse:[5]
