1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lars Piik, til Gåsevad=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Gunne Siggesson and Märitta Arvidsdotter Pik
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurids / Lars Piik to Gåsevad, Kungsbacka Kendt 28/4 1420 The first time we find "Gaazavadh" (Gåsevad) mentioned in documents is in 1406, when Enar Magnusson, on Euphemia-day the same year, issues a deed of sale for property in S
2 CONC weden to his nephew Gunne Siggesson. But the squire Lars Piik probably already owned the farm then, although he first appears in 1420 on 28 April in a deed of exchange between him and Thure Stensson (Bjelke), whereby he exchanges 
2 CONC for two farms in Tveta district, which he inherited with his wife Bengta, a daughter of Olof Boson (Oxehufvud), a mill and the village of Forss in Tölö parish, which village was henceforth subject to Gåsevadholm. Lars Piik had, ho
2 CONC wever, been married several years before, for in 1434 the wedding of his daughter Ingegærd to Karl Haka was celebrated at Gåsevad. He was married twice: 1) in 1409 at Tanum church to Gertrud Bosdotter, widow of Lasse Skytte, 2) be
2 CONC fore 1420 to Bengta Olofsdotter (Oxhufvud), daughter of Olof Bosson and Katarina Karlsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Pik, är 1458 väpnare, bosatt på Gåsevad i Halland. Han var gift två gånger: 1) 1409 med Gertrud Bosdotter, änka efter Lasse Skytte, 2) före 1420 med Bengta Olofsdotter (Oxehufvud), dotter till Olof Bosson (Oxehufvud) och [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/people/Katarina-Karlsdotter/6000000038310548435 Katarina Karlsdotter]. Denna Katarina Karlsdotter var nära släkt med Ebbe Pik och hans son Bengt Pik från den äldre Pikätten. Änka 1458, då hon på Kilagård till sin
2 CONC  måg Tule Nilsson och dotter Estrid sålde en gård i Skälleryd. Lagmannen i Västergötland, Bengt Gylta kallas då hennes systerson. 
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pik_(%C3%A4tt)_
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5sevadholms_slott
