1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sigvid Sigvidsson Ribbing (Skåne)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Sigvid Sigurdsson Ribbing, den Lange & a unknown wife
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvid Ribbing in Skåne; Called in Anna Bülow's Notice of Old Kindred Seved Ribbing; Where a Välboren lord of Skåne, who lived in 1345, who may have come from Norway in 1335; Is referred to as a strict and hard man; Considered the
2 CONC  ancestor of all Ribbingarne in Sweden, and with him Peringsköld begins his handwritten pedigree across the Ribbingska genus. - Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002192078283&photo_id=6000
2 CONC 000174632888841&position=0 '''Märta Ulfsdotter Hjorthufvud,'''] in her 1st marriage, born at the year 1320; In about 1353 to 1363 a strict Enlightenment for Queen Margaret in her younger years; † in Norway and where buried; daught
2 CONC er of the Knight and Svea Reich's Council and the Man of the Nerike Ulf Gudmarsson (Hjorthufvud or Folkunge), to Ulfåsa, who first carried a deer head with a neck, then his the mothers or the Folkungevapnet, a lion, with Brigitta 
2 CONC Birgersdotter or Sancta Brita (see Brahe, N: o 1) and married (2)  with Knight Knut Algotsson to  Hammarö, by the old Grip or Griphufvudslägen. Märta married Sigvard Ribbing in 1337 - "the wedding at Ulvåsa" (the wedding march of 
2 CONC the same name was composed by August Söderman much later). Mother Birgitta opposed the marriage because she disliked Sigvard Ribbing. The couple settled at Vapnö Castle outside Halmstad in Halland. Märta became a court mistress an
2 CONC d supervisor for Margareta Valdemarsdotter, when she as queen and wife of Håkan (Håkon) VI arrived in Norway and Akershus. Märta had a daughter, Ingegerd, who was raised together with Queen Margareta Valdemarsdotter. Ingegerd beca
2 CONC me an adult abbess in Vadstena monastery, but was removed from office, accused of forgery, embezzlement and frivolous conduct. Märta was also married to the knight Knut Algotsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peter Sigvidsson Ribbing,''' (dead in 1379), commonly called Peter Ribbing, is mentioned among King Albrek's followers in the stagnation treaty with King Magnus's followers in 1371. He became the Council of Ministers in 13
2 CONC 75 or 1376, made the 1379 pilgrimage to the Holy Land, wrote his will in Rome and died on his way home in Florence shortly after he became a knight. Married to Marshal Karl Ulfssons by Tofta half sister Kristina Ulfsdotter ( Sparr
2 CONC e av Tofta ) but died childless after inheriting her half brother Arvid Ribbing in Uppland drowned son Arvid Ribbing
2 CONT * 2. '''Arvid Sigvidsson Ribbing''' son of Sigvid Ribbing,  at Arms; Lived in 1390. - Married 1st with Ingeborg Magnusdotter, of old Stureätten, in her 2nd marriage; daughter of the Knights and the Council of Magnus Magnus Amundss
2 CONC on  (Sture) and widow of Ulf Nilsson, à Vapn, of whom she was given the morning gift of Hamneryd and Sundra farm and qvarn, but with whom she had no children: - 2: o with Brita Pehrsdotter; daughter of the Knight Pehr Sture. 
2 CONT * 3. '''Bengt Sigvidsson Ribbing,'''  lived in 1409
2 CONT * 4.  '''Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter,''' birth circa, 1360, married Peter Andersson Prika (stjärna), son of Anders Prika i Gällstad
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0375.html '''Von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3, page 371''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sigvid Ribbing in Scania;''' Called in Anna Bülow's Notice of Old Family Seved Ribbing; Where a well-born lord of Scania, who lived in 1345, who may have come from Norway in 1335; Referred to as a stern and hard man; Considered
2 CONC  the ancestor of all the Ribbings in Sweden, and with him Peringsköld begins his hand written pedigrees of the Ribbing family. - Married to Märta Ulfsdotter (Hjorthufvud), in her 1st marriage, b. In the year 1320; Was around 1353—
2 CONC 1363 a strict Adulterer for Queen Margaretha in her younger years; † in Norway and 
2 CONT buried there; daughter of Riddaren and Svea Rikes Råd  and Lagmannen i Nerike Ulf Gudmarsson  (Hjorthufvud or Folkunge), to Ulfåsa, who first carried in the weapon a deer head with a neck, then his the mothers or Folkungevapnet, a
2 CONC  lion, with Brigitta Birgersdotter or Sancta Brita (see Brahe, No. 1) and remarried with the Knight Knut Algotsson to Hammarö, of the old Grip- or Griphufvudslägten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peder''', à Vapn; Svea Rikes Råd; Was childless and in 1402 went with his wife to the holy tomb, but they were to die on the road. In 1375, as a pledge, the Second Council of Sweden sometimes confirmed a King Albrecht's Chart
2 CONC er; likewise in 1376 the King's letter to the dioceses in the kingdom stated: shall finally give Hamneryd (two farms in Ås) and Flateryds mill in Wadsbo district, which all he inherited from his nephew Arvid Ribbing, to Wadstena m
2 CONC onastery, according to a written record written in 1518, which Arvid Skeff, who was Ingeborgs, Arvid Ribbing 's wife Redesven, must have given Peder Ribbing is called by Catharina Knutsdotter (Griphufvud), in  his confirmation let
2 CONC ter for Wadstena monastery brother (half-brother). - Married 1360 to Christina Ulfsdotter; daughter of Riddaren, Riks-Råd and Lagmannen Ulfo Abjörnsson (Sparre, No. 7), to Tofta, with his 1st wife, Margaretha Sunesdotter (Bååt, No
2 CONC . 3). 
2 CONT * '''Arvid'''  (son of Sigvid Ribbing, Tab. 2), à Vapn; Lived in 1390. - Married 1st with Ingeborg Magnusdotter, of the old Stureätten, in her 2nd marriage; daughter of the Knight and Riks-Råd Magnus Amundsson (Sture) and widow of
2 CONC  Ulf Nilsson, à Vapn, of whom she received as a morning present Hamneryd and Sundra farm and mill, but with whom she had no children: - 2nd with Brita Pehrsdotter; daughter of the Knight Pehr Sture. Sons: Arvid; Drowned unmarried 
2 CONC in Upland &Peder; Svea Rikes Råd.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg''' Married Peter Andersson Prika, i Möne 
2 CONT * '''Bengt'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/6656 Ribbing, Related]
2 CONT
2 CONT More famous was '''Sigvid Ribbing''' (died not earlier than 1345), whose relationship to his older names does not preserve source data; according to a German chronicle, he was of the same genus as Knut Porse. He was chief whiteman
2 CONC  ("capitaneus") in southern Halland at least 1336–41 - perhaps as guardian of Knut Porse's sons - and by 1341 he '''married Märta Ulfsdotter (Ulvåsa family),''' the eldest daughter of Saint Birgitta. Birgitta was similar to R in a
2 CONC  robber, and according to the Chadstone abbot Margareta Clausdotter's (bd 25) chronicle of Birgitta's family he was very harsh and cruel (cf. the meaning of the word ribbing above). Hans and Märta Ulfsdotter's son Peter Sigvidsson
2 CONC  (d 1379), usually called Peter R, is mentioned among King Albrek's supporters in the standstill treaty with King Magnus' followers in 1371. He became the council of the council in 1375 or 1376, made the pilgrimage to the Holy Lan
2 CONC d in 1379, wrote his will in Rome and died on his way home in Florence shortly after he became a knight. R was married to Marshal Karl Ulfssons of Tofta half-sister Kristina Ulfsdotter (Sparre of Tofta) but died childless after in
2 CONC heriting her half-brother (Liedgren) Arvid R's in Uppland drowned son Arvid R.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigvid_Ribbing Sigvid Ribbing, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvid Ribbing was courtier over Halland and lord of the castle to Falkenberg Castle .
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvid Ribbing was a courtier in southern Halland 1336-1341. Nothing is known about his relationship, a German chronicle states that he was related to Knut Porse . Sigvid married before 1341 Märta Ulfsdotter (Ulvåsaätten) , daught
2 CONC er of Saint Birgitta . Saint Birgitta likened him to a robber and Vadstena abbess Margareta Clausdotter describes him in her chronicle of Birgitta's relatives as very harsh. Ribbing means traitor or violent man, which may be the r
2 CONC eason why he was given the nickname Ribbing. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage between Sigvid and Märta has later been linked to the story of the wedding at Ulvåsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Peter Sigvidsson Ribbing to Vapnö,''' gunsmith and councilor .
2 CONT * '''Arvid Sigvidsson Ribbing'''
2 CONT * '''Ingegerd/ Ingeborg  Sigvidsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvid Sigvidsson Ribbing, died about 1350. Lives in Vapnö castle, Halmstad. From the family Ribbing no. 15. Sigvid was born in the early 14th century. Through an inheritance in 1340, he received the estate Vapnö in Halland (Vapnö
2 CONC  belonged to the Ribbing family since the beginning of the 14th century). Sigvid was a courtier over southern Halland between the years 1330 and 1345. He is described as a cruel and hard man. Stayed in Norway and Sweden in 1335. S
2 CONC igvid married Märta Ulfsdotter in 1341. She was the daughter of Ulf Gudmarsson Hjorthufvud and Birgitta Birgersdotter (Saint Birgitta). Märta was only 13 years old when it was decided that she would become the wife of Sigvid Ribbi
2 CONC ng. The marriage was more of a "political agreement" between her father and the reigning King Magnus Eriksson than a happy marriage. Sigvid Ribbing who was a "robber" made himself rich through thefts from the ships in the Kattegat
2 CONC  between Denmark and Sweden. King Magnus Eriksson wanted power over trade in Sweden and in order to have a calm trade between the countries, he made a well-planned move by letting Councilor Ulf Gudmarsson's daughter Märta marry Si
2 CONC gvid Ribbing and persuade him to stay calm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Through the marriage between Märta and Sigvid, Ulf Gudmarsson also strengthened his position as an adviser to the king because the agreement with Sigvid Ribbing was a political success for King Magnus Eriksson. Marta's mother, Sai
2 CONC nt Birgitta, opposed the marriage between Märta and Sigvid. When Sigvid and Märta got married, Saint Birgitta did not want to attend the wedding at Ulfåsa but sat outside the wedding hall. After a while she regretted it and eventu
2 CONC ally she went to them in the hall at Ulfåsa (more about this can be read in Magdalena Ribbing's book - The Ribbing 700 years in Swedish history).  '''Märta and Sigvid were married for just over 10 years and had four children.''' S
2 CONC igvid Ribbing died in the early 1350s when the Great Depression ravaged Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Source: Elgenstiern. 
2 CONT * Source: Magdalena Ribbing's book - The Ribbing family 700 years in Sweden's 
2 CONT
