1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of King Charles VIII of Sweden and Kristina Abrahamsdotter
2 CONT * Anna, a natural daughter of Carl VIII  Knutsson and his mistress Christina, whom he explained to his real wife in 1470 on the cot. Anna married the chieftain at Westerås Castle in 1450   , Håkan Svensson Bölja. King Karl VIII's 
2 CONC  daughter Anna, can be found in Notes on Swedish women (Stockholm, PG Berg, 1864), now scanned at Project Runeberg. 
2 CONT * Karl Knutsson was born in October 1408 or 1409, at Ekholmen Castle, the son of Knut Tordsson (Bonde), knight and member of the privy council (riksråd), and Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta), the only daughter and heiress o
2 CONC f Charles Ulvsson, Lord of Tofta. His father Knut was first cousin of Erik Johansson Vasa's father. His first marriage, in 1428, to Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke) (died 1436) gave him his daughter Christina. His second marriage, in
2 CONC  1438, to Catherine (Gumsehuvud, died in 1450) produced his second daughter Magdalena, who married Ivar Axelsson (Tott). He also had two children by his third wife (and former mistress) Christina Abrahamsdotter, Anna and Karl. His
2 CONC  father was said by contemporary legends to descend from a younger brother of King Eric IX (Saint Eric). His mother, an important heiress, descended from Jarl Charles the Deaf and consequently from some ancient Folkunge earls of S
2 CONC weden, as well as from Ingegerd Knutsdotter, a daughter of Canute IV of Denmark and Adela of Flanders.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006588594080&photo_id=6000000118119715821&position=1 '''Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde) is listed in the Granfelt fran Dal - Mörner af Tuna, Volume 2, page 196 as the d
2 CONC otter of  King Karl Knutsson Bonde.''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006588594080&photo_id=6000000137033662839&position=0 '''Historical Geographical and Statistical Lexicon over Sweden / Third Band. GH / 542 Anna Karlsdotter (Bond
2 CONC e) is also listed as the dotter of  King Karl Knutsson Bonde''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006588594080&photo_id=6000000118119715821&position=0 '''Håkan Svensson (Bölja), chief white man at Västerås castle.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006588594080&photo_id=6000000118119715821&position=0 '''Christina Håkansdotter af Wangaslagten,''']  married Peder Pedderson, till Hagalsrum, son of Peder Hakans
2 CONC son, till Hagelsrum and Carin Gustafsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_VIII_of_Sweden Charles VIII of Sweden, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Early Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Knutsson was born in October 1408 or 1409, at Ekholmen Castle, the son of Knut Tordsson (Bonde), knight and member of the privy council (riksråd), and Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta), the only daughter and heiress of 
2 CONC Charles Ulvsson, Lord of Tofta. His father Knut was first cousin of Erik Johansson Vasa's father. His first marriage, in 1428, to Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke) (died 1436) gave him his daughter Christina. His second marriage, in 1
2 CONC 438, to Catherine (Gumsehuvud, died in 1450) produced his second daughter Magdalena, who married Ivar Axelsson (Tott). '''He also had two children by his third wife (and former mistress) Christina Abrahamsdotter, Anna and Karl.'''
2 CONC  His father was said by contemporary legends to descend from a younger brother of King Eric IX (Saint Eric). His mother, an important heiress, descended from Jarl Charles the Deaf and consequently from some ancient Folkunge earls 
2 CONC of Sweden, as well as from Ingegerd Knutsdotter, a daughter of Canute IV of Denmark and Adela of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With his wife Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke), Charles had:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ture Karlsson (Bonde)''' (died young before 1447)
2 CONT * '''Christina Karlsdotter (Bonde)''' (c. 1432 – before 1500), married 1446 to the noble, councillor, and courtier Erik  Eriksson (Gyllenstierna).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With his wife Catherine Karlsdotter, Charles had:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margaret Karlsdotter (Bonde)''' (1442–1462)
2 CONT * '''Magdalena of Sweden''' (1445–1495), married to noble Ivar Axelsson (Tott) in 1466
2 CONT * '''Richeza Karlsdotter (Bonde)''' (born c. 1445), nun at Vadstena Abbey
2 CONT * '''Bridget Karlsdotter (Bonde)''' (1446–1469), nun at Vadstena Abbey
2 CONT * '''Four sons died early'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With his Mistress Christina Abrahamsdotter, Charles had:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde),''' married to the noble Håkan Svensson (Bölja), governor of Västerås castle.
2 CONT * '''Charles Karlsson (Bonde)''' (1465–1488)
2 CONT
2 CONT
