1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Karl Karlsson Bonde=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of King Charles VIII of Sweden and Cristina Abrahamsdotter 
2 CONT * Karl, born a bastard but acknowledged in his father's will in 1470.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Karlsson_%28Bonde%29 Karl Karlsson (Bonde), by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Karlsson ( Farmer ) , born around 1465 , was the son of King Karl Knutsson (Farmer) and Queen Kristina Abrahamsdotter .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Arms of the Bonde Family.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl was legitimized as the real son of his father when, towards the end of his life, he married his former wife Kristina so that the son could inherit the throne. However, he was outmaneuvered by Sten Sture the Elder and never ca
2 CONC me into possession of more than parts of his paternal heritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT A person who is probably identical with him claimed in Stockholm's town hall in 1488 a number of valuables, which councilor Arvid Olsson kept for him until his death. This Karl Karlsson managed, with the support of a letter from S
2 CONC ten Sture, to have the objects handed over to his deputy Nils Sture , who probably handed them over to Karl. Johannes Magnus wrote that Karl "lived and aged in awful conditions".
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/mobil/Artikel/12366
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Harrison (2004), p. 415
2 CONT * Harrison, Dick (2004). Karl Knutsson: a biography . Swedish rulers. Lund: Historical media. Libris 9649091 . ISBN 91-85057-54-1
2 CONT
