1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Knut Tordsson Bonde==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Tord Röriksson Bonde and Ramborg Cecilia Nilsdotter (Vasa) 
2 CONT * Knut Bonde (son of Tord Bonde) died in 1413. Knight. Hövidsman at Turku Castle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 1408-09-20 with '''Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta),''' daughter of the council and march Karl Ulfsson ( Sparre of Tofta ) and Helena Israelsdotter ( Finstaätten ).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children with Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Karl VIII Knutson Bonde,''' born 1408, died 1470 King.  Karl Knutsson, King Karl VIII Knutson (son of Knut Bonde), born probably 1408, died 1470-05-15. King of Sweden 1448-06-20. Elected king of Norway in 1449. Lost his Norwe
2 CONC gian crown as early as 1450. Appointed king of Sweden in 1457, was recalled to the king in the autumn of 1464. Declared his crown in 1465. Again called king in 1467-09. '''Married 1: o 1429-02-28 at Ekholmen with Birgitta Turesdot
2 CONC ter (Bielke),''' daughter of the knight and the Swedish Council Ture Stensson ( Bielke ) and Birgitta Abrahamsdotter (bull head). Married 2: o 1438-10-05 in Stockholm with '''Katarina Karlsdotter (gumsehead),''' daughter of the Sw
2 CONC edish National Council Karl Ormsson ( gumsehead ) and Märta Gregersdotter (Aspenes ). Married 3: o 1470 with his dear Kristina Abrahamsdotter , possibly daughter of the chief of the Raseborg's western herd Abraham Pedersson (half 
2 CONC animal).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==List of Swedish Diplomatarium's Medieval Letters from sok.riksarkivet.se
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Knut+Tordsson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_22948&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 22948]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1438 March 24, of Issue Björnö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Krister Nilsson, killed in Sweden, who sued the general from Frötuna ship team before his farm Björnö, confirms with his judgment the four letters that Jöns Larsson in Ösbyholm previously received in the dispute between
2 CONC  him and Johan Jakobsson in Väsby, "Askarna Hærade", Frötuna parish, with several touching land in Väsby, and prohibits conviction of 40 marks for a royal judgment. The first letter was issued by one of 6 saviors and 6 peasants fr
2 CONC om three hard-headed people's national committees, the second by Nils Mattsson, deputy in Uppland, the third by Mr Knut Uddsson, Hans Kröpelin and '''Karl Tordsson Bonde''' and the fourth by Archbishop Jöns, who in the presence of
2 CONC  the national council, Mr Nils Gustavsson, the Uppland lawyer, Mr Knut Udsson, Hans Kröpelin, '''Karl Tordsson Bonde,''' Erik Nilsson in Visby and Erik Ingemarsson, district governor, sued the general from Frötuna ship team before
2 CONC  him at Skeppsholmen near Stockholm and confirmed all the letters that Jöns Larsson had before. Present at the event at Björnö were Mr Karl, church pastor in Frötuna, Karl Djäken, county governor and judge in Frötuna, and several 
2 CONC others. The letter issuer seals. A tergo: "co 59" - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001437731307?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140284259962
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Knut+Tordsson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=5&postid=sdhk_22744&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab  22744]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1437 May 2, of Issue: Hundred Shepherd's Court'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Kättilmundsson in Grävsta, judge in Lyhundra on behalf of '''Karl Tordsson Bonde,''' announces on county council in Lyhundra hardened on 10 ½ herring land in Penningby, Husby-Lyhundra parish, as Mrs. Ingeborg Magnusdotter in
2 CONC  Vänngarn, widow of Mr. Knut Uddsson, with her daughter's wife Märta's consent donated to the soul choir in Uppsala Cathedral, according to gift letter (1436 10/8 - SDHK no. 22630 ) which she had read on the thing. Witnesses were 
2 CONC church pastors Olof in Estuna and Peter in Lohärad.
2 CONT Fasters: Botvid in Vämblinge, Lars Andersson in Täby, Peter in Sätuna, Peter in Nodsta, Anders in Aspsund, Ragvald in Norrby, Jöns in Nyckeöby, Staffan in Torrvalla, Lars in Nora and Peter in Degarö. Sealants: '''Chief of Staff Ka
2 CONC rl Tordsson Bonde.''' - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001437731307?album_type=photos_of_me&end=&photo_id=6000000140284214956&project_id=&start=&tagged_profiles=
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Knut+Tordsson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=4&postid=sdhk_22465&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 22465]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1435 October 26, of Issue: Stockholm
2 CONT
2 CONT Archbishop Olof in Uppsala, bishops Tomas in Strängnäs, Sigge in Skara, Magnus in Turku and Olof in Västerås, the knight Krister Nilsson, slain in Sweden, the gunman Karl Knutsson, the national marshal, the knights Gottskalk Bengt
2 CONC sson, Nils Erengislesson, lawman in Sörmland , Lawyer in Närke, '''Karl Tordsson Bonde,''' Lawyer in Västmanland, Olof Ragvaldsson, Lawyer in Östergötland, Knut Jonsson, Lawyer in Västergötland, Bengt Jönsson, Knut Karlsson and al
2 CONC l the knights and souvenirs, the national council and the private knightship, saviors, clerks and clerks merchant townsmen and privates all over the kingdom declare that Hans Kröpelin has shown himself to be "a faithful dandeman" 
2 CONC and gives him his protection.  Sealants: Archbishop Olof in Uppsala, bishops Tomas in Strängnäs, Sigge in Skara, Magnus in Turku and Olof in Västerås, the knight Krister Nilsson, slain in Sweden, the gunman Karl Knutsson, the king
2 CONC dom's marshal, the knights Gottskalk Bengtsson, Nils Erengislesson, lawman in Bengt Stensson, Lawyer in Närke, '''Karl Tordsson Bonde,''' Lawyer in Västmanland, Olof Ragvaldsson, Lawyer in Östergötland, Knut Jonsson, Lawyer in Väs
2 CONC tergötland, Bengt Jönsson and Knut Karlsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
