2 CONT ==Magnus Marinasaon ätt==
2 CONT
2 CONT Speculations and facts.
2 CONT
2 CONT His ancestry is unknown. He might? HE MUST have been a son of a woman named Marina, or at least a stepson, period. She COULD have been [http://www.geni.com/people/Marina-Valdemarsdotter/6000000001897786984 Marina], daughter of Kin
2 CONC g Valdemar Birgersson. She was the only ''documented'' person in Sweden known to be called Marina in the 1200s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''....'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Yes his ancestry is unknown, but his mother, or stepmothers name must have been Marina, and when it comes to the linking to Marina Valdemarsdotter it gets very thin, she could earliest have been born shortly after 1260, thus have 
2 CONC been max 25 years old when she married the Noble Lord Rudolf II of Diepholz 1285, unless the dates are wrong, giving her a son with him, that oddly was knighted at only max 8 years old... a son that also before 1304 also have had 
2 CONC four children in his first marriage, meaning that he must have married at the age of 15... again, it doesn't hold up. 
2 CONT
2 CONT If  Marina Valdemarsdotter at the other hand only was his stepmother, the things becomes more plausible, unfortunately, Rudolf II of Diepholz has no known issue. he married [https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-von-Kleve/600000000382
2 CONC 7618351 Agnes von Kleve] 1275 shortly after her first husband had died, any children by her would earliest have been born 1276, it would better fit Magnus if she was his real mother, but unfortunately, there's no record of any chi
2 CONC ldren, anyway, she must have died before her second husbands second marriage to Marina before ca. 1285, but as Magnus is titled "dominus" already in 1293, he would only have been around 17 years old at that time which again makes 
2 CONC it less plausible. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To summon it up, the very idea that this mentioned Marina above was his mother is very unlikely, because it doesn't fit in chronological, nor is supported by any records or indirectly by any indications. The only thing about his a
2 CONC ncestry we actually do know, is the fact that his last name was Marinasson, thus a son of a woman named Marina.
