1 NAME Tönne /Oxehufvud/
2 GIVN Tönne
2 _MARNM Oxehufvud
2 NICK Tønnes
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Denmark
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1220
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Denmark
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE! Halland was Danish until 1720, when it became Swedish!
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Tönne'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Född:	cirka 1220
2 CONT * Död:	Halland, Sverige
2 CONT
2 CONT * Husband of NN NN 
2 CONT * Father of Per Tönnesson (Oxehufvud), til Hellerup 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/Baad/Brodersen.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Tönne Oxehufvud — Historical Profile
2 CONT Tönne Oxehufvud was a historical figure from Halland, Denmark, active in the late 13th and early 14th centuries. While the exact details of his life are limited, genealogical records indicate that he was born circa 1220 in Halland
2 CONC  and died circa 1258 in the same region MyHeritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and Lineage
2 CONT Spouse: Tönne married Maka Oxhuvud (born Bibali), who was born in 1225 MyHeritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: They had at least one son, Per Tönnessen Oxhuvud (also recorded as Per Tönnes Oxhuvud in some sources) MyHeritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name “Oxehufvud” appears to be a variant or related form of “Oxhuvud,” a common Scandinavian surname derived from Old Norse elements meaning “ox-hall” or “ox-hall-hall” (hall-hall), often indicating a place name or estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Context
2 CONT Halland, a province in southern Sweden (then part of Denmark), was a region of cultural and political significance during the medieval period. The Oxhuvud/Oxehufvud family appears to have been part of the local nobility or gentry,
2 CONC  as evidenced by their land-based surnames and recorded lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Resources
2 CONT For further genealogical exploration:
2 CONT
2 CONT MyHeritage provides family tree entries and variant name records for Tönne Oxhuvud, linking him to other historical figures in the Oxhuvud family MyHeritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Danish Family Search (Dansk Familie Søgning) offers access to church books, censuses, and other Danish historical records, which may contain more details about Tönne’s life and estate Danish Family Search.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rigsarkivet (Danish National Archives) and arkiv.dk host digitized parish registers, land records, and other archival materials that could provide additional context OnGenealogy+1.
2 CONT
2 CONT FamilySearch’s Denmark Church Records collection (1484–1941) may also contain later records of the family, though Tönne’s own records are likely in earlier parish registers FamilySearch.
2 CONT Summary
2 CONT Tönne Oxehufvud was a Halland-born nobleman or landholder in the early 13th century, married to Maka Oxhuvud, and father of Per Tönnessen Oxhuvud. His life and lineage are preserved in medieval Scandinavian genealogical records, a
2 CONC nd further details may be uncovered through Danish parish registers and land records.
