2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bonde_nr_11#TAB_5 '''Tord Bonde'''], born in the mid-1300s. Died 1417-03-21 probably at Viipuri Castle. Knight and counselor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married to '''Ramborg Nilsdotter,''' daughter of the ruler and Nils Kettilsson (Vaasa) and Chistina Jonsdotter (Rickebyätten).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Knut Bonde.''' Knight. Death 1413. See Tab. 6
2 CONT * '''Karl Bonde.''' National Council and Teamman. See Tab. 8
2 CONT * '''Margareta Tordsdotter,''' died in 1401. Married to the knight and the council, lvar Nilsson (pre-clad). [SBL: 5 s315]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Catalog of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gustaf+Johansson+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=8&postid=sdhk_10888&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab '''SDHK no: 10888''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 October 9'''
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: Nyköping''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Issuer: Spouses Nils Kettilsson and Kristina Jonsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Kettilsson, together with his wife Kristin Jonsdotter, bequeaths to his brother-in-law Tord Bonde and his wife Ramborg, the testator's daughter, and both of their heirs 13 öresland of land in Norsa in Norrsunda parish, 13 öre
2 CONC sland of land in Skalmsta in Skånela parish, 12 öresland of land in Norrby in Vidbo parish, 9 öresland of land in Bergby in the same parish and 4 1/2 örtugland of land in Rävsta in St. Olofs parish (later in Odensala parish) in Si
2 CONC gtuna for 150 marks of soldered silver, which Tord Bonde paid in full. None of the issuers' heirs shall after this day be able to exchange or revoke these properties, or any part of them, as long as Tord Bonde and his wife Ramborg
2 CONC  are not reimbursed the paid silver sum within six months after the estate has been deeded. Kristin Jonsdotter specifically certifies that she approves of the sale because the properties are her rightful parents. The issuers furth
2 CONC er give district chiefs and sheriffs (in the areas where the land is located) power of attorney to give their brother-in-law Tord Bonde or his representative title to the properties on their behalf in accordance with national laws
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SEAL''' The issuers seal together with the knight Karl Ulfsson of Tofta and Bo Jonsson, drots in Sweden. Only four seal strips remain with a wax fragment at No. 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Additional text:''' On the back: Niclis Kætils ons br[ e ]ff d e‑ po Norusa ‑e pa Skalnustade / f‑ Norsoo and Norbẏ y Widhbo sok e n and Berghbẏ j bi d em / and j gardh ij Ræffsta widh Sicthuna ij S anc te Ol o ffs sok e n ‑f
2 CONT Printed DS 9337  see pdf of print Printed regest RPB no. 1224  FMU no. 873  Listed in List 1561 of Gustaf Johansson's (Tre roros) land deed, published by KH Karlsson in Västergötland's Fornminnesförenings Tidskrift 2, booklet 8-9 
2 CONC (1908), p. 168.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Literature and Commentary:'''  For the letter's trading via Cecilia Stenbock's archive in Haga, see L. Sjödin in MRA 1943, p. 58. About Nils Kettilsson (Vasa) and his wife see H. Gillingstam, Ätterna Oxenstierna och Vasa und me
2 CONC deltiden (1952), pp. 158 ff. (this letter mentioned p. 167 f.) and ÄSF 2, p. 103 f. About Tord (Röriksson) Bonde see SBL V, p. 315 ff. Compare Tord Bonde's deed of gift 1378 8/9 (RPB no. 1368, SDHK no. 11301 ) on the properties to
2 CONC  his wife Ramborg, in which it appears that the transfer in the present letter to Tord Bonde constituted compensation for a debt. See S. Rahmqvist, "Skånela before Skånelaholm" in Skånelaholm. An estate in Uppland (Sidén 2008). SD
2 CONC HK No. 11301
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr:  [http://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=peter+israelsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=11&postid=sdhk_16101&tab=post#tab 16101]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elin Elofsdotter in Kundby sells to Tord Bonde Röriksson 2 marks of land in Kundby, Rimbo parish, Sjuhundra herad in Uppsala diocese, with all houses and lands, fields and meadows, forest and fishing water, etc. for 300 marks of m
2 CONC oney. Sealed by Karl Ulfsson of Tofta, Philpus Karlsson, Jöns Finvidsson, Nils Kurka, Magnus Israelsson, Nils Markusson, Laurens church priest in Rimbo and Peter Torstensson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [http://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Tord+R%c3%b6riksson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_17020&tab=post#tab 17020]
2 CONT
2 CONT Old' Mr. Tord Bonde Röriksson issues letters at Tullgarn in Vagnhärads sn, Södermanland, Odensvi (in Viby sn) ​​in Närke and others. estate there, which his son Mr. Knut Bonde gave his wife Margareta as a present tomorrow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [http://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Tord+R%c3%b6riksson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_44212&tab=post#tab 44212]
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bonde Röriksson to the council in Reval with a request for help for a citizen named Staffan to collect his claim in Reval.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [http://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=100&Sokord=Tord+R%c3%b6riksson+Bonde&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=37&postid=sdhk_18792&tab=post#tab 18792]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rd Tord Röriksson Bonde submits a certificate that the Russians wrongfully took Mr. "Symmer"'s estate, which belonged to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT = Tord Bonde, by Wikipedia=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bonde From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search Lord Tord Röriksson, nicknamed Bonde, Lord of Penningby (born in 1350s, died 21 March 1417, Toordh Bonde in his era's Eastern Norse language; Tord Bonde 
2 CONC in today Swedish) was a medieval Swedish magnate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bonde was born into the highest nobility of his era's Sweden. His parents were lord Rörik Tordsson (of the Bonde) and lady Märta Gisladotter (of the so-called Sparre of Aspnäs). Tord Bonde was married to lady Ramborg Nilsdott
2 CONC er (of the Vasa family).
2 CONT
2 CONT Quite young, he was entrusted with the position of castellan of Raseborg, Finland. He was knighted and appointed a Royal Councillor. Later, he allied himself with Queen Margaret I of Denmark and benefited from being her trusted ag
2 CONC ent. In 1403 lord Tord received an appointment as chatelain of Viipuri castle and county, at which office he would serve until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1404, he started to launch offensives against Russians that led to a new treaty. In September 1408, hostilities opened again. Tord Bonde fought the Russians by, for example, using sea piracy against their commerce. In 1409 agai
2 CONC n a new treaty brought further advantages to the Swedish. Around 1411 Russians, having felt Viipuri a haven of hostile actions and aggression, launched an attack. Most of the town was destroyed. However, the castle did not surrend
2 CONC er, the besiegers ultimately retreated, and peace was restored.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Knut Bonde died in 1413, a couple of years after having had a son of his own, Charles Knutsson (1408-70), who would become King of Sweden in 1448. Tord's second son was Karl Bonde, and Tord's daughter Margareta Tordsdotter
2 CONC  married lord Ivar Nilson. His other grandchildren included Tord Carlsson Bonde the marshal, and lady Ingeborg Ivarsdotter, who would become mother of five of the Tott Axelssons.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
