1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Karl Ulfsson Sparre av Tofta 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ulf Abjörnsson (Sparre av Tofta) and Kristina Sigismundsdotter 
2 CONT * Born in the 1300s, buried in Vadstena monastery February 17, 1410 was a Swedish knight , national council , marshal and lawman in Uppland and grandfather of King Karl Knutsson .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Ulfsson(son of Ulf Abjörnsson). Studied in younger days in Paris. Appeared in the records at the earliest in 1349. Became a knight for some of the years 1354-1358, possibly in the summer of 1355. Mentioned as district governo
2 CONC r in Trögd 1354-11392, as councilor from 1356. Was the chief in Uppland possibly as early as 1359 and is certainly mentioned as such 1362 - 1405. Was march 1364–1371, surrendered at Stockholm Castle 1364–1365, and chief white man 
2 CONC at Viborg from the 1380s to 1399. Died 12–18.11 1407 about 90 years old. Received 1361 Dåvö kingsgård in Munktorps sn in Snevringe hd in Västmanland in lifetime extension. Had a time Björkekind's HD in Östergötland in pledge. Had 
2 CONC a time in Köping County. His main estate was Tofta in Adelsö snow in Färentuna hd, to which he always subscribed, and Ekholmen in Veckholm snow in Trögd hd, both in Uppland, and he also held it from half sister Kristina inherited 
2 CONC Fågelvik.The genus of the Algot Sons ) daughter Birgitta, second time most recently 28.9 1363 with Helena, who is said to have died by 1375 and was the daughter of the landowner Israel Birgersson ( Finstaätten ) and probably Bengt
2 CONC a Karlsdotter (Färla, Oreste Keldorsson's family ), third time with Cecilia, and fourth time with a woman by name unknown, who survived the man for a short time and was buried with him in Vadstena monastery 17.2 1410.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Knut Karlsson,''' Appeared in the records for the first time in 1375 and was already a knight. Mentioned as national council from 1376, as governor of Gästrikland 1379, as lawman in Södermanland 1380-1386. Appears still 11.8 
2 CONC 1388. Seems to have fallen in Västergötland at the beginning of 1389. Owned property in Åkerbo hd in Västmanland, in the east of hd in Östergötland, in Mo hd in Småland and at Lederne near Stockholm. Mr. Knut died childless and wa
2 CONC s probably unmarried and inherited by his father.
2 CONT * '''Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta)''' Buried in Vadstena Monastery 15.3 1429. Inheritance after her was held 28.2 pp. '''Married for the first time around 1408 to the knight 'Knut Tordsson Bonde,''' who is buried in Vads
2 CONC tena monastery 1413, in which she married the mother of King Karl Knutsson, and '''married the second time 1414 to Sten Turesson ( Bielke ),''' who then married Agneta Eriksdotter ( Krummedige ) and is buried in Vadstena monastery
2 CONC  8.9 1431.
2 CONT
2 CONT == List of Swedish Diplomatarium's Medieval Letters from sok.riksarkivet.se
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_6374&tab=post#tab 6374]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1352 May 7, of Issue: Tofta
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta)''' gives his wife Ingrid Eriksdotter in the morning gift farm Strandby (Kungs-Husby parish, Trögds county), property in Staby and Grönsö, Bond-Arnö parish (Trögds county), with all the preparation
2 CONC s. The knights were the knights Karl Näskonungsson, Rörik Bonde, Karl Ulfsson and Filip Ragvaldsson, the canyon Johan Karlsson in Uppsala and the canyon Birger Gregersson in Strängnäs, the weapons Verner van Kyren, Finvid Finvidss
2 CONC on, Karl Törnesson, Bengt Fadersson, Svens Fadersson and Birger Nilsson.  Nils Abjörnsson, Puke Glysing, Erengisle Sunesson, Bengt Algotsson, Margareta Sunedotter seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/6374.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=3&postid=sdhk_7360&tab=post#tab 7360]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 May 23, of Issue: Stockholm
2 CONT
2 CONT King Erik issues letters of protection to the brothers in the Sigtuna Dominican monastery and assigns to '''Mr Karl Ulfsson of Tofta''' to assist in litigation and other matters and, upon request, give their subordinate due reprim
2 CONC and.
2 CONT The issuer seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/Sdhk_7360_7360.jpg#?c=&m=&s=&cv=&xywh=0%2C-2079%2C4367%2C7068
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=
2 CONC true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=40&postid=sdhk_8012&tab=post#tab 8012]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1361 August 22, of Issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus donates his farm Dåvö (in the parish of Munktorps) to '''Mr Karl Ulfsson of Tofta,''' and his wife that along with the county income is held with all royal rights in their lifetime. The farm's guardian is hereby notifi
2 CONC ed. The issuer seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/8012.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=11&postid=sdhk_8620&tab=post#tab 8620]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1364 November 14, of Issue: Stockholm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karl Ulfsson of Tofta,''' knight and marshal of King Albrekt of Sweden , testifies to himself and his heirs that he received from King Albrekt and his father Duke Albrekt, Stockholm's castle on faith and the law and not as a pl
2 CONC edge, with the obligation to return the castle upon request. to King Albrekt, Duke Albrekt or their heirs. As a fellow pledgee, his relative the knight Drost van Stove stands.  The issuer and Drost van Stove, knight seal. - https:
2 CONC //sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/8620.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=140&postid=sdhk_13685&tab=post#tab 13685]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Dating: 1390 February 12, of Issue: Ekholmen
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The knight Karl Ulfsson of Tofta''' donates to the councilor in Stockholm, Herman Svarte, his inherited estate Knut's inherited estate in Liderne, which after Herman's death will go to the Helgeandshuset in Stockholm.  The issu
2 CONC er seals and asks the mayors and councilors in Stockholm to seal with the city seal. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/Sdhk_13685_13685.jpg#?c=&m=&s=&cv=&xywh=0%2C-2079%2C4367%2C7068
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=179&postid=sdhk_16839&tab=post#tab 16839]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1407 February 21, of Issue: Mariuborg
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Staffansson (Ulv) sells to '''Mr Karl Ulfsson to Tofta''' all the inheritance that accrued to him after Mr Harald Karlsson (Stubbe) in Kastlösa on Öland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&Innehall=%22karl+ulfsson%22+tofta&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaR
2 CONC egest=true&EftermedeltidaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=180&postid=sdhk_17449&tab=post#tab 17449]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1410 March 2, of Issue: Vadstena
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Knut Bonde and his wife Margareta Karlsdotter acknowledge that the Vadstena monastery obtained the right of disposal for their lifetime to the farms "Klaesstad" and Ekby, who was donated to the monastery by '''Karl Ulfs
2 CONC son of Tofta,''' and his sister wife Kristina Ulfsdotter, , Kristina's mother, testament to the same monastery, comprising the farms Brånäs, Ekenäs and Hannäs in Dagsbergs sn, Torrö in Hammarkind's hd, Motala, land on Öland, and S
2 CONC källnora mill in Uppland. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/Sdhk_17449_17449.jpg#?c=&m=&s=&cv=&xywh=0%2C-2079%2C4367%2C7068
2 CONT
2 CONT == Karl Ulfsson (Saved by Tofta)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Knights, Riksdag, Riksråd'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta), born circa 1317, d 17 (Messenius) Nov 1407. Parents: Swedish National Council Ulf Abjörnsson (Sparre av Tofta) o Cristina Sigmundsdtr (3 clover leaves). Studied law in Paris (Sankt Nikolaus' by Link
2 CONC öping canonization process), artium mag there (Messenius), mentioned in Sweden at the earliest 49, hieradsh in Trögd in Uppland at least 54-92, knight some of the years 54-56, council at least 56-96, the Uppland troll from 58 or 5
2 CONC 9 certainly 62–05, the national director 59, joined in Sthlm 64–65, March 64–71, the chief white man at Viborg at least 87–99.
2 CONT
2 CONT G 1) 6 May 1352 m Ingrid Eriksdtr, dtr to Erik Boberg and Birgitta Knutsdtr (family of the Algot Sons); 2) no later than 1363 m Helena Israelsdtr, d no later than 1379 o troll no later than 1375, dtr to the Council of State Israel
2 CONC  Birgersson (Finstaätten; bd 16) o troll Bengta Karlsdtr (Färla; Oreste Keldorsson's family); 3) m Cecilia, d Oct 5 (year unknown); 4) m a to the name unknown, who survived K, buried in Vadstena 17 Feb 1410.
2 CONT
2 CONT K is stated at his death to have been about 90 years, thus born about 1317, which corresponds to the fact that the parents could not be co-located at the earliest in 1318 and the father together with the grandfather in 1317. - Unl
2 CONC ike his uncle Nils Abjörnsson, K joined King Magnus' son Eriks rebelled in 1356 and was then named as one of his council. That he became one of Erik's foremost followers is evidenced by a commentary from about 1400 on some of St. 
2 CONC Birgitta's revelations. According to this, Erik's widow Beatrix (bd 2) of Brandenburg was pregnant at his death in 1359. In anticipation of the child's birth, K is said to have become governor for the short time that elapsed until
2 CONC  Beatrix died and the little son was excised from her body but died the same day.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a 16th-century record in Bishop Hans Brask's family book, K must have been one of the leaders of those who killed Duke Bengt Algotsson (bd 3), King Magnus' favorite, against whom Erik's rebellion was primarily directe
2 CONC d by the proclamation with which the rebellion started in 1356. According to the same 16th century record, Bengt Algotsson had previously been married to K's half-sister Ingeborg Ulfsdotter but displaced her. According to the Visb
2 CONC y Chronicle, the murder of him must have taken place in 1360 in Rönneholm in northwestern Skåne.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the reconciliation between King Magnus and his son Håkan, K was among the seven national councils who in 1362 according to the Visby Chronicle were banished to Håkan against his father. Via Gotland they then went to Mecklenb
2 CONC urg. This became the prelude to Albrekts by Mecklenburg's ascension in Sweden and K's appointment in 1364 to march and joined in Sthlm. In a letter of April 20, 1365, he mentions how he "quarreled" with the kings Magnus and Håkan 
2 CONC in Gataskogen in western Uppland. The former had been captured there on March 3, 2006. Ks marshal's title indicates that he was there commander of King Albrek's army. After the stagnation in Edsvik in Sollentuna between, on the on
2 CONC e hand, Albrekt, on the other Magnus and Håkan in 1371, at which K is mainly mentioned among Albrekt's followers, he has not been able to occupy this title (cf. Vol. 4, p. 147, o. 29, p. 524). ff). During negotiations with the Han
2 CONC seatic cities of Tönsberg in 1372, Magnus and Håkan argued that K and his colleague Bengt Filipsson (Ulv), now called traitors (proditores) and enemies (inimici), were removed from their territory, where they were apparently priso
2 CONC ners; In 1375, it was stated that this happened outside the harbor of Marstrand (Die Recesse ... der Hansetage) - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/6252
2 CONT
