1 OCCU Riksråd
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Erik Karlsson (Vasa)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 	Son of Karl Kristiernsson (Vasa) and Ebba Eriksdotter Krummedige 
2 CONT * Erik suffered a bloody death in 1491; while travelling, he and his entourage gatecrashed a priest outside Strängnäs. In the scuffle with the priest and his people, Erik himself was mortally wounded. (Source: Lars-Olof Larsson - 
2 CONC Gustav Vasa - father of the country or tyrant?)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his brother, Kettil, in 1465, Erik became the family's portal figure during the turbulent and bloody power play of the following years. With several castle counties in his hands, mainly Stäkeholm and Rumlaborg i
2 CONC n northern Småland, Erik had a strong position. After Karl Knutsson Bonde was reinstated as king, Erik allied himself with Christian I, who made a concerted action to regain the Swedish crown. But with the defeat in the Battle of 
2 CONC Brunkeberg in October 1471, Erik was also on the losing side. He therefore entered into a settlement with the victorious National Superintendent Sten Sture. Erik kept his place in the Riksråd, but was never knighted.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the 1470s and 1480s, Erik Karlsson, together with Erik Axelsson Tott, was one of the main commanders in the defense of Finland against the Russians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik suffered a bloody death in 1491; while travelling, he and his entourage gatecrashed a priest outside Strängnäs. In the scuffle with the priest and his people, Erik himself was mortally wounded. (Source: Lars-Olof Larsson - Gu
2 CONC stav Vasa - father of the country or tyrant?)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Vasa#TAB_4 Royal Family Vasa, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (TAB 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik Karlsson to Norrby born 1436, † 1491 in Överselö. Was killed by Church- ruler Sigfrid in Överselö when he wanted to force him to death in Överslö prästgård. Hövitsman at Stekeholm, Knight and Riksråd. Never dubbed knights.
2 CONC ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Married 1: o before 1466 with Iliana Nilsdotter Oxenstierna,'''  † 1481-1488. Daughter of the Knight, Riksrådet and Nils Jönsson Oxenstierna and Katarina Karlsdotter Sture . 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Married 2: o about 1488 with Anna Karlsdotter Vinstorp,''' buried 1552-05-01 in Dalum's church, Redvägs hd in her 1st wedding . Her 2nd married 1493 with the council and the knight Erik Eriksson Gyllenstierna , † 1502, the de
2 CONC ath penalty. Daughter of the Swedish Council Karl Bengtsson Vinstorpaätten and Karin Lagesdotter Gustav Mattsons ätt .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children in 1st married to Iliana Nilsdotter Oxenstierna=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Karl,''' † as a child.
2 CONT * '''Kettil,'''  † as a child.
2 CONT * '''Johan Eriksson,''' † as a child.
2 CONT * '''Several daughters,''' † as a child.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Child in 2nd married Anna Karlsdotter Vinstorpaätten =
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Karl Eriksson,''
2 CONT * '''Margareta Eriksdotter,''' † around 1541-44 in Germany. Married 1: o before 1515 with Erik Knutsson Tre Rosor , † executed in Stockholm's bloodbath 1520-11-04. Married 2: o 1523-10-14 in St. Lars Church in Söderköping with the
2 CONC  Knight, Berend von Melen Council , † 1561-09-02 at Herbsleben in Thuringia.
2 CONT * '''Ebba Eriksdotter,''' † 1549-11-22 in the Vreta monastery and was buried November 30 in Linköping. Married 1512-01-19 in Söderköping with the knight and the council Erik Abrahamsson Leijonhufvud , † executed in Stockholm's blo
2 CONC odbath 1520-11-04. Their daughter Margareta got married to Gustav I Vasa .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://nobles.narod.ru/vasa.htm The House of Vasa in Sweden and Poland, Descendants of Nils Kettilsson (VASA)]
2 CONT
