1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ban%C3%A9r_nr_22#TAB_2 '''Anders Isaksson, till Östanå'''] i Riala socken, Stockholms län. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Squires.''' Mentioned in letters 1405–1445-01-18. Was a member of the royal council, when he participated in the Kalmar meeting 1438-07-09.
2 CONT * [https://www.spottinghistory.com/view/2499/ostana-castle/ '''Östanå estate'''] is mentioned in 1433 when it was owned by Anders Isaksson Baner. Since them it has been a residence for Fleming and Wrede families. The wooden main b
2 CONC uilding from 1680s was burnt down by Russian army during the Great Northern War in 1719. The current manor house was built in 1791-1794 by Simon Bernhard Hebbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Ingegerd Svensdotter (Pik),''' who was alive 1444-07-01, daughter of the squire Sven Pik, who carried a gray-white clam on a red field, and Cecilia, daughter of the Mecklenburg knight Gise van Helpten.
2 CONT
