2 CONT '''Lawman, Knight, Council of Ministers'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birger was the son of the knight Per Israelsson. Birger Persson was the weapon of two lowered wings.
2 CONT * Born in 1266 at Finnstad, Uppland, Sweden. 
2 CONT * Death:  April 03, 1327 in Uppland, Sweden.
2 CONT * Sridhar P (also Birger Petersson to Finsta, died 1327, was Swedish Greatman, Knight, Privy Councilor, Upplands first Lawspeaker and co-author To the Uppland law and the father of Saint Bridget. Birger was the son of the knight P
2 CONC er Israelsson. Birger Persson was the weapon of two lowered wings.
2 CONT * The same year, he changed the farm Finsta towards Skällnora Gård in tempt parish which becomes his new farm until he re-switches to him Finsta by a change with Magnus Nilsson (Ivar Nilsson's methodof Villberga In Villberga Paris
2 CONC h.
2 CONT * Birger was one of the people who witnessed the Dukes ' Testament, which was established on 18 January 1318. Following the death of the Dukes in 1318, he, along with Mats Kettilmundsson, took the lead in the rebellion against Kin
2 CONC g Birger, which led to the election of Duke Erik's Three son Magnus the following year. Birger received on 13 December 1320 the farm Algö in Överselö in the gift of the Duchess Ingeborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Mobil/Artikel/14142#/Sbl/Mobil/Artikel/16041 (1) '''Kristina Johansdotter''']  (The family of the Elof Sons) in Uppland,  who lived July 6, but was dead July 11, 1293. Their marriage was c
2 CONC hildless. About her see bd 13, and AF Liljeholm in PHT 1952 -
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married; [https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birger_Persson_(Finsta%C3%A4tten)  (2): '''Ingeborg Bengtsdotter  Folkungaättens'''] They had  seven children (Gardell, 1, no 159), four of whom apparently died early.  She lived in 1294 
2 CONC at Gotland østre, Sweden. She died at Nærke, Uppland, Sweden. Records show Birger Petersen Was married Ingeborg Bengtsdotter of Folkungaättens.. Ingeborg was the daughter of teammate Bengt Magnusson (Folkungaättens teammate) and S
2 CONC igrid the fair . She died in 1314.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Ingeborg Bengtsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Israel Birgersson (Finsta)''';  the Riksrådet, the lawyer in Uppland, the knight Israel Birgersson, Israel Birgersson, lagman Birger's son, had three children, of which Ramborg, Peter certainly, and Helena  in Mr Israel's fam
2 CONC ous married. Of these, Ramborg Israelsdotter became 1) m Filip Nilsson (troll Sparre of Tofta) and 2) m knight, the national council and the lawyer Anund Jonsson (Lion's face) as well as Helena Israelsdotter with the knight, the n
2 CONC ational council, the marsh and the lawyer Karl Ulfsson (Sparre of Tofta). Israel Birgersson's son Peter Israelsson dy is little known. He was present as King Håkan's followers at Edsviken in 1371 and was not a knight. Peter's esta
2 CONC te had been withdrawn by King Albrecht; Peter was last named as alive November 23, 1379 and buried in Vadstena Monastery March 24, 1384 (diarrhea). With him, Birger Petersson assumed the line. Married to Bengta Karlsdotter (Färla)
2 CONT * '''Per Birgersson,''' died  young
2 CONT * '''Bengt Birgersson,''' died  young
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Birgerdotter,''' died young
2 CONT * '''Margareta Birgerdotter,''' died young
