1 NAME Magnus /Knutsson (Aspenäs)/
2 GIVN Magnus
2 SURN Knutsson (Aspenäs)
2 _MARNM Knutsson (Aspenäs)
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1299
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 6 JUL 1366
1 OCCU Lagman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Magnus Knutsson (Aspenäs) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Knut Jonsson (Aspenäs) and Katarina Bengtsdotter (Folkungaätten) 
2 CONT * Magnus Knutsson (Son of Knut Jonsson, tab. 3). First appeared 17.5 1335. Knight became some of the years 1336 — 1340, probably by King Magnus Coronation 21.7 1336. Was vicelagman in Östergötland 1340. Board as a Privy Council on
2 CONC ly in a letter of year 1351 and then together with several persons, who also only mentioned as a Privy councilor. Was lawspeaker in Östergötland 1347 and even 1363. Would have been deprived of his lagmans dignity in connection wit
2 CONC h King Albrekts of Mecklenburg enthronement, since Nils Jonsson (Rickebyätten) 22.8 1364 called himself Östgötalagman. Is 6.2 1366 again lawspeaker in Östergötland, when he also the last time appear as alive. Was probably dead 6.7
2 CONC  1366, because Bo Jonsson (Grip) was then Östgötalagman. Be sure dead 1369. He and his brothers Fråntogo's: Take clear monasteries in Stockholm Earth in Långhundra, Trögds and Vaksala HD in Uppland, which their father Knut Jonsson
2 CONC  1333 had given to the monastery with their sister Ingeborg. King Magnus Eriksson awarded the 1348 monastery this earth until further investigation has been done about the matter. Was 24.11 1350
2 CONT * Magnus Knutsson, Knight, Councilor, lawspeaker in Östergötland. Son of Drotsen Knut Jonsson (Aspenäsätten). Knutsson first appeared on 17 May 1335, and was knighted sometime between 1336 and 1340, probably at Magnus Eriksson 's 
2 CONC coronation on July 21, 1336.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: Helga Bengtsson, who was the daughter of Bengt Eales, according to A. F. Labra obviously Birger Jarl's nephew (Brunkow Ekeby), and widow at least since 12.10 1339 after Tiohäradslagmannen Sune Jonsson (boat, Erengisl Su
2 CONC nasons). Begrossed 8.1 1393 in Vadstena monastery. She received from Sune Jonsson Earth tomorrow's gift in ash HD in Östergötland, which she, when the marriage was childless, donated to Vadstena monastery and got after him soil in
2 CONC  eastern HD in Småland and owned in other soil in S. Vedbo and Western HD in the same landscape , as well as in Ash, Dals and Valkebo HD in Östergötland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Adel Weapon Wiki - Aspenäsätten - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Aspen%C3%A4s%C3%A4tten
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Birgitta Magnusdotter'''  married Biskopsmördaren Mats Gustavsson (Sparre).  Lived 28.8 1398 but buried 7.9 pp. In Vadstena monastery. Inherited Edshult in similar snow in Södra Vedbo hd in Småland. Was first married to Mils
2 CONC  Sverkersson ( Stubbe ), who died before 1369. Was 27.3 1379 married to the knight Mats Gustavsson ( Sparre, Mats Gustavsson's family ), when this mortgaged estate, which belonged to Nils Sverkersson. Mr. Mats appeared in 1374 in 
2 CONC connection with the murder of the link-opening bishop Gotskalk and was buried in 1419. He was 11.6 1410 married to Birgitta, daughter of Halsten Petersson (boat) and Katarina Svensdotter (sparrow). Mrs. Birgitta Halstensdotter was
2 CONC  married to Nils Jonsson ( Bååt) after Mr. Matt's death.), who first appears on March 15, 1435, the last time on August 14, 1440, and is mentioned dead (Death Act) 7.1 1441, when his wife lived widowed after him.
2 CONT * '''Katarina Magnusdotter av Aspanes,'''  d. Abt 24 Aug 1393, Lived another 24.8 1393. Received at inheritance after his father Ekolsund in Husby-Sjutolfts sn in Trögd hd in Uppland and all his goods in Uppsala bishopric. She tra
2 CONC ded land in Norra Vedbo hd in Smaland. Owned land in Färentuna hd and Danderyds skplg in Uppland. Was 1,91373 married to the Swedish National Council Finvid Finvidsson ( Frössviksätten ), who appears in the sources 1351-1388 and w
2 CONC as previously married to a daughter of Gustav Arvidsson ( Sparre av Vik ).
2 CONT * ''' Ingeborg Magnusdotter [Aspenäsätten],''' Was dead December 6, 1389. Tranås inherited in Säby sn in Norra Vedbo hd in Småland and exchanged land in the same hd. Was married to Magnus Karlsson (eagle foot), who appears 1355 –1
2 CONC 362.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==History==
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1340 he becomes Vicelagman in östergötlands Lagsaga. In a letter from 1351 he is mentioned as Privy Councilor. He was lawspeaker in Östergötland 1363, something that may have deprived him with Albert of the Mecklenburg Enthrone
2 CONC ment, since Nils Jonsson (Rickebyätten) 22 August 1364 called himself Östgötalagman.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 February 1366 he is again lawspeaker in Östergötland, when he, according to known tasks, occurs for the last time in the annals. He probably died before 6 july 1366 when Bo Jonsson (Grip) was lawspeaker in Östergötland. Surel
2 CONC y he was dead 1369. [citation needed] Magnus Knutsson owned the land in Bankekinds and Trögds hundreds In Uppland and in Dalsland in Östergötland. He married Helga Bengtsson (winged arrow) on 24 November 1350.
2 CONT
