1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Kettil=
2 CONT
2 CONT * THIS IS NOT A Fictitious Person:
2 CONT * IF THE SON IS KETTILSSON THE FATHER IS KETTIL.
2 CONT * This is so far known and he should hence stand here as it is the last known ancestor.
2 CONT * Vasaätten, Swedish savior family, finally royal dynasty in Sweden and Poland.  Already in the 14th century, there were three special families in Roslagen with the coat of arms, which from Gustaf I's time, due to gradually changi
2 CONC ng form, was called "the vase". That they were related to each other and formed branches of the same tribe is for many reasons very plausible. Two of them were already extinct during the Middle Ages, without having really succeede
2 CONC d in rising from the class of the provincial lowland nobility. The third, on the other hand, also seems to have belonged to the lower savior at first , but was counted from the first half of the 15th century. to the country's fore
2 CONC most noble families. Its first, authoritatively certified member was the gunsmith Nils Kettilsson, who is mentioned in 1361-78 (see V. 1). A son of his was the Crown Prince Kristiern Nilsson (see V. 2), among whose sons and grands
2 CONC ons several took a prominent political position during the final stages of the Middle Ages (see V. 3-9). 
2 CONT
