1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jöns Laurentii=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Lasse Garp and Elin Ragvaldsdotter Ulfsparre af Broxvik
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=12289 Jöns Laurentii, Dean, Chancellor]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Laurentii, still alive in 1537. Parents: Lasse garp and Elin Ragvaldsdtr (Fargalt). Kanik in Uppsala no later than 7 Jan 01 with Bondkyrka (Holy Trinity), Upps, as prebend from between 13 June 09 and 1 Dec 12 to 31 July 19 an
2 CONC d then Rasbo, Upps, Gustav Eriksson's (Vasa) chancellor at least from 9 April to between 9 o 28 May 23, dean in Uppsala from between 9 o 28 May s å, acting archbishop about SEK 1 June 29—Aug 31.
2 CONT
2 CONT J was the nephew of the lawman in Södermanland Peder Ragvaldsson (Fargalt) and the lawman in Norrfinne lagsaga Erik Ragvaldsson (Fargalt), both councilors and deceased in the 1490s (vol. 15). His ancestral land was in western Öste
2 CONC rgötland (Liedgren 1957), and a sister of his was prioress in Skänninge nunnery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In political contexts, J first appears in 1503 as an envoy from the Swedish National Council to Erik Turesson (Bielke; vol. 4) in Viborg and in 1504 as an envoy to Novgorod. In the summer of 1516, he represented the Uppsala domcha
2 CONC pitel at the meeting in Södertälje together with the domprovost Kristofer Lintorp and Erik Geting (bd 17). From a letter from Jakob Ulvsson to Sten Sture dy it appears that J shortly afterwards visited Nyköping, which was held by 
2 CONC Sten Kristiernsson (Oxenstierna), who was accused of stamping with Kristian II and Gustav Trolle. This and J's later fate have led to a presumption that it was J who revealed the stamps to the superintendent (Wieselgren), but the 
2 CONC basis for this conclusion has been considered fragile (Westin). Since Sten Sture began to besiege the Fence in the fall, J acted as an envoy between the domchapitel and it, and in the spring of 1518 he represented it again during 
2 CONC negotiations with the reichspriest, now together with two other canons. When Sten Sture and about twenty of his main followers agreed in 1519, following a petition from Gustav Trolle, to answer for their actions in Rome, J appears
2 CONC  in the summons as the only accused from the Uppsala court chapter. After the death of the head of state, on March 20, 1520, before Gustav Trolle, he had to make a written abdication and renounce his seat and sue in the judicial c
2 CONC hapter, but was allowed to retain the canon title and Rasbo prebend.
2 CONT
2 CONT The war of liberation meant that J's antecedents came to be regarded as merit. Receipts from the autumn of 1522, from several occasions in the spring and summer of 1523 and even in the summer of 1524 testify that he was active in 
2 CONC the collection of silver for the amortization of the debt to Lübeck, including from several upland parish churches. From J's title in these receipts, it appears that in the spring of 1523 he was Gustav Eriksson's (Vasa) chancellor
2 CONC , from which office he however resigned, when he was shortly afterwards promoted to dean in Uppsala (Carlsson). Occasional grim letters to him from Gustav show that J sought to assert church interests to a certain extent. However,
2 CONC  he came to remain one of the king's confidants. After the new archbishop Johannes Magnus left the country and the dean of Uppsala Jöran Turesson (Tre roros) rebelled, J was authorized in 1529 by the king to "govern and rule" the 
2 CONC archdiocese in the archbishop's place with the help of Erik Geting. At the archbishop election in 1531, he was one of Laurentius Petris's three competitors but, according to Peder Svart, received the lowest number of votes, only t
2 CONC hree against Laurentius Petris's more than a hundred.
2 CONT
2 CONT J wrote his will in 1536 (tr of Peringskiöld) but was still alive in 1537, when he together with the judicial chapter authorized Peder Galle (bd 16) and Johannes Ek (bd 12) as representatives at the church meeting in Strängnäs (Kj
2 CONC öllerström 1931).
