1 OCCU Häradshövding, Väpnare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ulfsparre_af_Broxvik_nr_9#TAB_1 '''Måns Påvelsson, till Broxvik'''] och Förenäs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Var väpnare''' 1508. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Förde 1519''' endast en Sparre i vapnet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Häradshövding''' i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norra_Vedbo_h%C3%A4rad Norra Vedbo härad] 1520. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Uppräknas bland''' det rusttjänstskyldiga frälset i Småland 1526 och 1528. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Han skall hava''' pantsatt mödernegodsen till borgaren i Vadstena Lars Persson 1523, men de återlöstes av sonen Erik Månsson, som fick Viste häradsrätts fastebrev på Broxviks gods 1546, onsdagen före S:t Botolfs dag (16/6). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift''' med '''Elin Larsdotter''' (Bölja från Västbo), dotter av väpnaren [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%B6lja_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo '''Lars Svensson, till Ljusfors''' (Bölja från Västbo)], och hans 1:a fru Elsa Bengtsdott
2 CONC er (Ållongren).<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT = Måns Påvelsson Ulfsparre af Broxvik=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Påvel Tufvesson and Elin Ragvaldsdotter (Fargalt)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ulfsparre_af_Broxvik_nr_9 Noble family Ulfsparre af Broxvik no. 9, Old salvation family, introd. 1625]
2 CONT
2 CONT Through Jonas Bång's work »Den hög- och welborna Ulfsparre-slächtens ättaretal» (Sth. 1755), the proud line of paternal ancestors of the family has entered the knight house genealogy, starting with a Geriche, who lived in the year
2 CONC  980 and must have been either »king over Värmland and Dalarne» or »lord over Värend in Småland». The absurdity of the oldest genealogies should be easy to see, all the more so as only four genealogies are stated to have lived for
2 CONC  three whole centuries. But even from the beginning of the 14th century, when our records become more numerous, the genealogy is not much more certain. All the searching for a Knut Abjörnsson, a Måns Knutsson, a Jöns Månsson marri
2 CONC ed to his niece, who could with the slightest hint of probability be included within the Ulfsparre family, has been as fruitless as for the "distinguished" Swedish surname Bjugg. Everything that is reported about this family befor
2 CONC e Måns Påvelsson, who lived at the beginning of the 16th century, whose living circumstances and marriage are known, seems to be only a tissue of the most unreasonable poems, in which one or the other true but not belonging inform
2 CONC ation has entered as if by mistake. Måns Påvelsson's father is said to have been Pavel Månsson, knight of the Order of St. Brita (!), as was his father the governor Måns Påvelsson. What is certain is that the first-mentioned Måns 
2 CONC Påvelsson's mother was Elin, a daughter of Ragvald Magnusson (Fargalt), and who her husband was, a letter dated 11/12/1467 (in the national archives) informs about this, in which Ragvald sells property to his daughter Elin for 150
2 CONC  mark sw. money, or the amount she received this morning as a gift from her husband Paval Tufvason. From this it is clear that wife Elin's father-in-law was not named Måns but Tufve. With this, the strangely constructed genealogic
2 CONC al structure collapses, and all the previous generations from Geriche, who lived in 980, to Måns Påvelsson Bjugg, knight of the Order of St. Brita in 1441 and governor of Rumlaborg in 1452, must thus be removed from the Ulfsparres
2 CONC  family genealogy.
2 CONT It is possible that Påvel Tufvesson came from Denmark, as the name suggests. This is also stated by the fifteenth-century genealogists Olof Claesson and Rasmus Ludvigsson, who, however, call him Påvel Abrahamsson and make him the 
2 CONC son of an Abraham Påvelsson, who came from Holstein or Denmark. It is not known if and which coat of arms he wore. Perhaps he was only a "reasonable man". The son Måns Påvelsson was married to Elin Larsdotter (bölja), whose grandm
2 CONC other Elin Jönsdotter belonged to the Häggasönner family, who carried the distinguished coat of arms of a Sparrow over a leaf in the shield, which coat of arms was taken up by the Ulfsparre family. Måns Påvelsson's seal always sho
2 CONC ws only a Sparrow, but it is clear that this is merely a transitional form to the sparrow over the leaf, which family mark appears in his sons' seals. In addition, these placed as a helmet ornament an ascending wolf, probably the 
2 CONC same ascending animal, which appears on the helmet in the seal of their great-grandfather's great-uncle, the district chief Birger Jönsson. That this coat of arms was not the ancient ancestors of the Ulfsparrars is also evident fr
2 CONC om the fact that the Hjortö family, who later entered the knight's house, were allowed to keep theirs right down to the smallest detail, to shield and helmet with the Ulfsparrarn's perfectly matching coat of arms and also bear the
2 CONC  same surname without any protests. Such would certainly not have occurred if both families had not been aware that the weapon came from the same direction, and that thus one had no better right to the same than the other.
2 CONT The family, of which branches sometimes called themselves Ullberg and Norberg, has branched into the baronial family Ulfsparre af Broxvik .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ulfsparre_af_Broxvik_nr_9 Ulfsparre of Broxvik no. 9]
2 CONT
2 CONT TAB 1
2 CONT Påvel Tufvesson ( overview tab 2). Possibly of Danish birth. His weapon is unknown. Married approx. 1467 with Elin Ragvaldsdotter , daughter of the armsman Ragvald Magnusson (Fargalt) and Katarina Svensdotter Pik (mussel). For the
2 CONC  morning gift, 150 marks sw. money, which she received from the husband, her father sold her on 11/12/1467 three eighths in Hæraborum (Herrborum) in St. Anna's parish, Östergötland county and also gave her, on certain conditions, 
2 CONC one eighth in the same property. She exchanged these on 1498-02-01 with her son's consent for two farms in Broxvik (now Västanå) in Gränna parish (which thus came into the family) and Förenäs in the same parish (now part of Östanå
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Måns Påvelsson''' , to Broxvik and Förenäs. Was a squire in 1508. Brought 1519-11-08 only one Sparre in the weapon. District chief in Norra Vedbo district 1520 2 . Enumerated among the freedmen liable to service in Småland in
2 CONC  1526 and 1528. 1 He is said to have pledged the mother's estate to the burgher of Vadstena Lars Persson in 1523, but they were redeemed by the son Erik Månsson, who received the Viste county court's fasting letter on Broxvik's es
2 CONC tate in 1546, the Wednesday before St. Botolf's Day (16/6). '''Married to Elin Larsdotter , daughter of the gunsmith Lars Svensson (bølja) of Ljusfors, and his 1st wife Elsa Bengtsdotter (ållongren).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Lars Månsson ,''' to Ruda (Council) in Skärstad parish. Lived in 1544.
2 CONT * '''Anna Månsdotter ,''' lived 5 1619-05-07. Married to farmer Lars Jönsson .
2 CONT * '''Erik Månsson Ulfsparre''' . Stand holder. Died 1564. See Tab. 2.
2 CONT * '''Elin Månsdotter ,''' lived 5 1619-05-07. Married to farmer Per Jonsson to Bohult in Gränna parish. She and her sons Jöns Persson to Ruda, Abjörn Persson to Näs in Gränna parish and Töres Persson to Bohult and their co-heirs i
2 CONC n Östergötland sold Bohult to wife Estrid to Broxvik and her co-heirs in 1596. 3
2 CONT * '''Jöns Månsson .'''
2 CONT * '''Göran Månsson .'''
