1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Karl Haraldsson Lake=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Harald Björnsson Lake, till Malma and Märita Bengtsdotter (bjelke, belagd med 3 stjärnor) 
2 CONT * Karl Lake. To Såtenäs, Tun (R). Covered from 1430, died in 1463. (Elgenstierna; see SD hk no. 21441 and SD hk no. 28057)
2 CONT * In 1439, a certificate is issued in Högsäter (P) that Karl Lake was not involved in the death of Erik Johansson in the Färgelanda tract. (Valley Dip 113)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lake_nr_53 Noble House Lake No. 53, Adelsvapen Geneologies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karl Lake (son of Harald Lake, Tab. 1),''' to Malma. Was a gunner 1430-08-01. Obtained at the inheritance after the parents in 1432 Såtenäs in Tun parish, Skaraborg county. Was dead in 1463. '''Married 1st to Cecilia Torbjörnsd
2 CONC otter, daughter of Torbjörn Jonsson (gumsehufvud) in Slätte and Ingrid Björnsdotter (a sea leaf). Married 2nd to Catharina Bengtsdotter, died probably before 1474, but certainly before 1479-02-23.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Harald Lake,''' District Chief. Died 1509. son of Karl Lake, Tab. 2), to Malma. Bought a farm with a mill stream in Malma parish in 1476 from his aunt Ingrid Haraldsdotter, who in 1478 transferred to him her right to 40 marks
2 CONC  of Malma church, which her mother had given there. Made a land exchange in 1485 with his mother's (stepmother's?) sister Bengta Bengtsdotter, widow of Peder Bertilsson (Liljehök). Was district chief in Barne district in Västergöt
2 CONC land in 1492 and again in 1497. Died in 1509, when succession was carried out after him. Married to Ingrid Nilsdotter, who lived in 1497, daughter of the squire Nils Pedersson (arrow), to Gåsevad in Tölö parish, Halland County and
2 CONC  Märta Larsdotter Pik.
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Karlsdotter ,''' Married to the squire and district chief in Asa district Bengt Björnsson (sparre), died after 1497, to Ulvstorp in Sparlösa parish, Skaraborg county, which property he already owned in 1483.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Catalog of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT
