1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Arvid Knutsson (Sparre över stjärna)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Knut Arvidsson, till Torpa (Drake af Intorp) and Kerstin Bengtsdotter (Kompan, chevron over leaves), Nr. 82 
2 CONT * Arvid Knutsson carried a chevron over a star in his weapon and is sometimes called Arvid Knutsson (Drake af Intorp) today . He was born in 1445 , died in the early summer of 1497 , and was a Swedish councilor , lawyer and distri
2 CONC ct chief during the Middle Ages.
2 CONT * Arvid Knutsson (son of Knut Arvidsson), to Torpa and Intorp as well as Lina in Väckelsångs parish, Kronoberg County and Tofta (Toftaholm) in Dörarps parish, Kronoberg County, which he received through his marriage. Born in the 1
2 CONC 440s. Called a prosperous sven in 1470, when Sten Sture authorized him to extract some forged gold, which was stored in Holtsljunga church (Vff. II h. 2-3, p. 9.). Sten Stures joined Kalmar Castle in 1472–1481 (Sb IV.). Obtained t
2 CONC he attorneys general's certificate in 1478, that he made clear and correct account for himself during the time he served him. Squire. Teamman 1475-97 in Tiohärad's law saga, Chief of Staff 1483-91 in Kind to his death and the Swed
2 CONC ish Council already (Sb V.) 1482-06-17, but probably at the same time that nan received the teammanship after the deceased Erik Eriksson (Gyllenstierna) in 1477. Chief of the Kinds district. Chief officer at Öresten some time duri
2 CONC ng the year 1490 and from 1493 until his death. One of Sweden's representatives at the Swedish-Danish peace meetings in Lödöse 1494 and 1496 and in Kalmar 1495 (Sv. Treaties, island). Death in early summer 1497 (Vff II h.2-3, p. 1
2 CONC 1.). He had the still-standing "stone house" built on Torpa and expanded the property through the acquisition of Kattagården in Torpa erected in 1485 and by Kvettatorpet 1495 (Hs.).   
2 CONT * Arvid Knutsson Drake; Cavalry captain. Adopted his modem name, but kept his federne weapon, See adal. family Drake of Hagelsrum
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82#TAB_4 The Noble Family of Drake by Intorp, Nr. 82]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000005033832835?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000174835394840 '''Anna Göstafsdotter, Stenbock'''] 1477-08-25 (morning gift) at Toftaholm (RHKn.) in her 2nd marriage (married 1
2 CONC st 1474-09-12 on Lina (G.Djurklou, About Göran Månssons to Bolmsnäs jordbok, p. 51 note 7.) with the Swedish National Council and the knight Fikke Göstafsson [Snedbjälke]), died in 1508 before 24/9, when succession was held after 
2 CONC the spouses (G.Djurklou, About Göran Månssons to Bolmsnäs landbook, p. 51 note 7.), daughter of the knight and the national council and the chief of the Älvsborg Göstaf Olofsson ( Stenbock, older family ), to Tofta and Erikstad, a
2 CONC nd his 1st wife Ingrid Bengtsdotter ( Vinstorpaätten ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Olof Arvidsson (Stenbock),''' Armed Forces and District Chief. Died in 1508. He took up his maternal arms and became the progenitor of the younger Capricorn family. See the wonderful family Capricorn .
2 CONT * '''Bengt Arvidsson, Squire,''' † before 1526, Married uncertain to whom 1489, when he issued a now-lost morning gift letter. Dead childless.
2 CONT * '''Knut Arvidsson,''' Arms, Chief of Staff. Death before 1526 childless. (But married)
2 CONT * '''Gustaf Arvidsson,''' dead childless about 1536.
2 CONT * '''Kerstin Arvidsdotter,''' married to the gunman Claes Hansson ( Uggla ).
2 CONT * '''Estrid Arvidsdotter,''' married before 1508 with the gunman and the commander-in-chief Peder Månsson ( Stierna ).
2 CONT * '''Märta Arvidsdotter,''' lived in 1558. Married before 1508 with the gunman and the district chief in Västbo hired Olof Drake .
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Arvidsdotter,''' lived in 1529. Married to the bailiff in Western and Southern Vedbo hd Nils Bagge ., Lived at Äpplaholm in N. Sandsjö sn (Jönk.), † 1530.
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Catalog of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gylta&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=25&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_37742&tab=post#tab '''37742''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1515 June 5''' 
2 CONT * '''Place of issue: Tofta'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Gylta and Anders Andersson announce a settlement reached between Arvid Knutsson's children about the inheritance after their father and mother in the presence of Seved Ribbing, Lindorm Ribbing and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17618 Dragon, Relatives, by Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 11 (1945), page 396.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake, savior families from Småland and Östergötland. Mainly in Småland appear during the late Middle Ages two low-saved families, in the literature called Sunnerbo-Drakarna and Västbo - Drakarna . The former included a. Magnus Bi
2 CONC rgersson Drake(still living 1465, was d. 1474) to Kalvnäs in Högsby sn (Kalm.), bailiff at Stäkeborg 1427, district chief in Aspeland and Sevede 1448 (cf. Svea Court of Appeal Liber causarum 60, no. 6, National Archives), Another 
2 CONC branch owned from the end of the 14th century to into the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the family, which was already disputed in an inheritance process in 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactorily inve
2 CONC stigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this family would possibly descend the noble family, which was introduced in 1646 and then became called Drake af Torp and Hamra (proba
2 CONC bly extinct in 1709); the baptismal name Christer used in the latter generation, however, rather indicates kinship with Västboätten. Colonel Johan Christersson Drake af Torp and Hamra belonged to the family, who fell in the battle
2 CONC  of Landskrona in 1677. His children include the lieutenant colonel, Fredrik Drake (b. 1660), who fell in the battle of Pultava in 1709 and is mentioned in Heidenstam's short story »Poltava» in »Karolinerna», and Sophia Drake (d. 
2 CONC 1741 ), gm Lieutenant Colonel Jon Stålhammar and in literature known as the one sung by Snoilsky in »Svenska bilder» «Frun på Salshult». - Västbo-Drakarnas (weapon: flying dragon) ancestor Kristiern Drake is said to have married M
2 CONC argareta Krumme, widow of the district chief Olof Jönsson (older Stenbocksätten). The son Olof (Kristersson) Drake was for a long time and still in 1518 district chief in Västbo. His grandson in the equestrian master Olof Nilsson 
2 CONC Drake (d. 1590) - on the father of the family (coat of arms: chevron over star) s that still survives in. the noble family Stenbock - took the name D., and the family branch introduced 1625 and extinct 1635, is known as Drake af I
2 CONC ntorp . About Olof Nilsson's father's cousin ,, Councilor Arvid Knutsson ;, (d. 1497) and his son the gunsmith and district chief Olof Arvidsson (d. 1508), who took up the maiden weapon (Capricorn), see Capricorn. Olof Kristersson
2 CONC  D: son (Olof Nilsson D: uncle) Arvid Olofsson Drake (d. After 1532), bailiff in Allbo and östbo, was the father of Märta Arvidsdotter, b. Around 1550 m. Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand); cf. Hand , relatives. Their son the gov
2 CONC ernor Arvid Knutsson Drake (d. Trol. 1618) took the mother's name and became the ancestor of the family Drake af Hagelsrum, see this. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17619
2 CONT
