1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Håkan Ragvaldsson (Båt av Billa)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ragvald Håkansson (Båt av Billa) and Elin Håkansdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=H%C3%A5kan+Ragvaldsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_22716&tab=post SDHK no: 22716]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1437 February 24, Place of issue: Exebo''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Armsman Håkan Ragvaldsson sells to well-born Björn Olsson his share in Tigerstad, Mörlunda parish.
2 CONT Exp. and Birger Trolle seals.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:'''  Post-medieval copies:  B 15 fol. 169v RA 0202, Printed regest SMR 520
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A5t_av_Billa Boat of Billa, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Boat of Billa is a name for a family that carried a boat in the coat of arms and whose manor was called Billa.
2 CONT
2 CONT The oldest known member of the family is Ragvald Håkansson who, together with his wife and with the consent of his father Håkan, issued a letter in Virserums sn, Aspelands hd in Småland in 1401.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref:
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Ragvaldsson (probably son of Ragvald Håkansson) is mentioned in 1409. He lived in Virserum in Virserums sn, Aspelands hd in Småland. Coat of arms: boat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mats Håkansson (probably son of Håkan Ragvaldsson) is mentioned in 1743. He was possibly married to a niece or nephew of Nils Turesson (Balk of Billa). Coat of arms: boat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Matsson (son of Mats Håkansson) lived in 1533 at Billa, Hemmesjö sn, Konga hd in Småland. He probably died before 1535 because he is missing from the military service records for this year. He is buried in Hemmesjö church. H
2 CONC e was married first to Ingrid Nilsdotter, daughter of Nils Jönsson (Halvhjort av Älmtaryd). He remarried to Elins Svensdotter, niece of Lindorm Mattsson (Läma).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources[edit | edit wikitext] Almquist, Jan Eric (1957). Wernstedt Folke. ed. Båt av Billa. Äldre svenska frälsesläkter: ättartavlor. Bd 1. H. 3. Stockholm: Riddarhusdirektionen. pp. 218-222. Libris 12871
