1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elin Svensdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Död efter 1511-06-12. Levde omkring 1500 i Rottne, Sörarby (G).
2 CONT
2 CONT * One might wonder if Rosenblck believes that the reason my opinion about Häkan Matsson's two marriages and about his sons' relationship with Lindorm Andersson is shared by Hans Gillingstam and the city archivist in Linköping Bo P
2 CONC ersson is that, like me, they think and believe without knowledge. Bo Persson, who had noticed the Bät av Billa debate on Anbytarforum, sent me a copy of an excursus for his C-thesis in history at Uppsala University on 10 October 
2 CONC 1983 with Professor Sten Carlsson as supervisor. His opinion is expressed in several places in the excursus and is illustrated by an extensive family tree, of which the part that includes the descendants of Lindorm Matsson's (Läma
2 CONC ) sister is reproduced here:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elin Svensdotter is mentioned in Bishop Hans Brask's family book (published by Hans Gillingstam and Göran Setterkrans, Sthlm 1968 - returns in Genealogica 2 in RA)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''However, from preserved source material it appears that Nils Lindormsson's father was called Lindorm Andersson and was a farmer in Rottne village in S. Rottne sn (now Söraby) and that his father was Anders Olsson (a non-savior f
2 CONC armer) and his mother '''Elin Svensdotter''' (a niece of the savior [https://www.geni.com/people/Lindorm-Matsson-L%C3%A4ma/6000000053894032826 Lindorm Matsson Läma])''
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: http://aforum.genealogi.se/discus/messages/576/367460.html?1275847119
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Pedersdotter-Bielke-af-%C3%85ker%C3%B6/6000000005736055391 Anna Pedersdotter (Bielke)], who was a cousin of the Danish nobleman [https://www.geni.com/people/Nils-Hogenskild/6000000006899789776 Nil
2 CONC s Hogenskild], stated in her family book from the 1540s that Iliana was Nils Hogenskild's mother, and that '''Iliana''' and '''Elin''' were nieces of [https://www.geni.com/people/Lindorm-Matsson-L%C3%A4ma/6000000053894032826 Lindo
2 CONC rm Matsson Läma]. In addition, she mentioned that Elin was the grandmother of Nils Lindormsson (Bååt). (Stig Östensson)
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the key documents for Stig Östensson's conclusions that Elin was married to Håkan Matsson - and not to his father - is Nils Birgesson's letter from 1552 about the estates Tingsryd (now Tingsryd municipality) and Tingsmåla (
2 CONC Tingsås sn, Tingsryd municipality), which Elin Svensdotter in Rottne and her sister Iliana in Hult had sold or mortgaged to Bishop Ingemar (mentioned in 1506 as bishop of Växjö).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Anders Olsson''' around 1500
2 CONT
