2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Iliana Håkansdotter.'''
2 CONT * '''NN Håkansdotter Båt av Billa.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: https://www.abc.se/~m8449/Naima2/004/00/385.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=36755&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_36755&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 36755]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Issued: 15100613, Växjö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: Kirstin Klängsdotter, Gunnar Skalle's widow, and Elin Svensdotter admit to having received payment for their property in Hagaby, which they sold to Mr. Erik Turesson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=37003&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_37003&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 37003]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Issued: 15110612, (Växjö)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: Cyrstyn Nelsadotter av Högnalöff authorizes her son-in-law Sven Jonsson in Söderköping to demand and collect the proceeds of her estate and farms in Östergötland. Anders Olsson's "Elyn" likewise authorizes her son-in-law 
2 CONC Sven Jonsson to speak on her behalf, especially regarding the estate that Bengt Abjörnsson has taken from her.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: https://www.abc.se/~m8449/Naima2/004/00/385.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=%22Sven+Jonsson%22&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=25&postid=sdhk_36570&tab=post#tab SDHK-nr: 36570]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Issued: 15090903, Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Updated Information=
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: Sven Jonsson with his wife '''Eline Svensdotter''' and the consent of his next of kin sells to Svante Nilsson and Mätta Ivarsdotter two of his and his wife's farms Östrebode and 2 "occupied" farms below and a salmon strea
2 CONC m, all in Bredevik parish, Kåkind district in Västergötland. Sealed by the issuer, Nils Svensson, Holger Karlsson, Johan Arendsson and Nils Bese
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Gillingstam's efforts in 1962 and 1965 were steps towards a final solution to the problems with the marriage of Mats Hakansson (Bät av Billa) and his son Häkan Matsson and the mothers of the latter's children. In a review of 
2 CONC the sources in 1962, he assumed "for lack of a better source" (than Uttter's guess) that Häkan Matsson had a full brother named Lindorm, and concluded that Mats Häkansson must have been married to Lindorm Matsson's (Läma) niece El
2 CONC in Svensdotter, which had the consequence that "the relationship with Nils 'Turesson's (balk) family seems to be difficult to investigate. "In 1965, when Jan Liedgren drew his attention to the letter in Gustaf lis's registry from 
2 CONC 1538, according to which Lindorm was called Andersson and not Matsson, Gillingstam writes: "If one assumes that Lindorm Andersson was the son of Elin Svensdotter in the marriage with Anders Olsson instead of in the marriage with M
2 CONC ats Häkansson (Bät av Billa), this would explain why Lindorm is not mentioned in a later story about Hakan Matsson's (Bät av Billa) brothers, and also appears in the jordeböckemna only after their death and therefore must have bee
2 CONC n considerably younger than them." He stated that Lindorm was probably Häkan Matsson's younger half-brother.In 1974, the definitive solution to the problems came through a letter in Gustaf lis's registry from 1552, about which I i
2 CONC nformed Hans Gillingstam. The letter is referred to by Professor Lars-Olof Larsson in Det medeltida Värend (1964), p. 377, note 47t, as follows: "Bishop Ingemar and the cathedral buy from 'Nils Hogenskilt's aunt' two farms in Ting
2 CONC sryd and Tingsmala. During the time of Bishop Jöns Bosson, they were bought by Arvid Hakansson to Billa even though he lacked birthright. In 1552 they were reclaimed by Nils Hogenskilt."? In another letter of 15/10 1588, which Gil
2 CONC lingstam was already aware of in 1962, and which I mention NV7, man Nil ia genian,2007, Nils Lindormsson (Bäảt, Lennart Nilsson's family), states that Anders Svensson (Sträle af Ekna) was"bördeman" to four farms, one of which, in 
2 CONC Ramsjo, is recorded as Nils Lindormsson's inheritance, while Hemmesjö, Frostensmála and Torsàs kvamn 1562 are reported under his recently deceased guardian Nils Hogenskild, who was his father's cousin (son of his grandmother Elin 
2 CONC Svensdotter's sister wife lliana in Hulta),'"Bördeman" was Anders Svensson on behalf of his mother-in-law Iliana Häkansdotter (Bát av Billa), who had the same mother, Elin Svensdotter, as Nils Lindormsson's father, Hans Gillingsta
2 CONC m's early knowledge of this letter contributed to his immediate conclusion from the information in the above-referenced letter from 1552 in Gustaf I's registry that Arvid Häkansson (Bät av Billa) belonged to "another family" than 
2 CONC Lindorm Andersson's mother Elin Svensdotter, that Arvid Häkansson was the only one of Häkan Matsson's children who had Ingrid Nilsdotter (Halvhjort av Almtaryd) as his mother, something that also agrees with what is stated in thre
2 CONC e family tables by their contemporary Bishop Brask. Elin Svensdotter was the mother of his second child, who was therefore Lindorm Andersson's younger half-sibling. The difficulty of investigating a possible relationship between H
2 CONC äkan Matsson and the Balk av Billa family, which supported Gillingstam's assumption in 1965 that Häkan Matsson and Lindorm Andersson were half-brothers, did not exist, which is why he could present a reasonable hypothesis regardin
2 CONC g such a relationship in the Bât av Billa family tree in Aldre suenska frälsesläkter 1:3. Gillingstam did not publish his interpretation of the 1552 letter. and in the Bät av Billa family tree, reference is therefore made to my pr
2 CONC esentation in Personhistorisk tidskrift 1974:1, pp. 40-43 with the same interpretation, which of course does not mean that he was influenced by me, as Rosenbalck, incorrectly and offensively to him, states. Finally, I would like t
2 CONC o comment on Niclas Rosenbalck's attempt on 6/2 2000 to "prove" that Lindorm Svensson's (Bock af Näs) child's grandmother's father Olof Häkansson (Bät av Billa) had the same mother as Arvid Hakansson, Ingrid Nilsdotter (Halvhjort 
2 CONC av Älmtaryd). He uses a tapestry dated to the 1620s, which is described in Personhistorisk tidskrift 1903. It is provided with 16 coats of arms and has belonged to some of Lindorm Svensson's (Bock af Näs) and Märta Ribbing's child
2 CONC ren. The coats of arms of this child's grandmother's grandparents depict Häkan Matsson's (Bät av Billa) coat of arms, a bät, and a half-deer, the coats of arms of Häkan Matsson's first wife. Since the coat of arms of the second wi
2 CONC fe Elin Svensdotter - if she had any - is unknown, can one be sure that the coat of arms intended for the wife contains it? I have chosen to quote this brief but precise summary, which differs greatly from the strange interpretati
2 CONC ons of the letter that Niclas Rosenbalck is guilty of on Anbytarforum on 16/1 2000 and 12/4 2010, in order to fit his"standpoint & question" since 1999. A somewhat more detailed summary could look something like this: "Nils Hlogen
2 CONC skid's 'aunt in Rotne' sold the estate "longt tilförcane' to bishop Ingemar in Växjö (bishop 1494-1530) with the possibility for the seller's relatives to "lose thet igen um thet förmodde. From bishop
