1 NOTE Lovet til Hertug Heinrich af Mecklenburg, men --
1 NOTE Bliver som 16 σrig gift med den 10 σrige Ludwig af Brandenburg, s°n af Kong Ludwig af Bayern
1 NOTE She was the founder of the Kalmar Union.  After her father's death, she 
2 CONT had her young son, Olaf, elected king of Denmark and governed in his 
2 CONT stead, as she also did in Norway after her husband's death in 1380. When 
2 CONT Olaf died in 1387, she was elected head of state in both countries; at the 
2 CONT same time she had her grandnephew, Eric VII of Pomerania (1382-1459), 
2 CONT acknowledged as her heir. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret faced opposition abroad from King Albert of Sweden (circa 
2 CONT 1340-1412) and the count of Holstein, as well as from the encroaching 
2 CONT Hanseatic cities. Many of the Swedish nobles, however, supported her 
2 CONT against Albert, who was finally defeated and deposed in 1389; the Swedes 
2 CONT then accepted Margaret as their queen. As head of the three realms, she 
2 CONT had Eric crowned king of Denmark and Sweden in 1397 (he had been accepted 
2 CONT as king of Norway in 1389) and had a treaty signed at Kalmar that created 
2 CONT a union of all three countries. This was the first time the Scandinavian 
2 CONT lands were joined under one king. Even after Eric came of age, however, 
2 CONT Margaret retained the reins of government. She made great efforts to 
2 CONT amalgamate the three realms, ruling with a firm hand that strengthened 
2 CONT royal authority. She died while campaigning against Holstein. The Union of 
2 CONT Kalmar lasted nominally until 1523, when Sweden broke away. Denmark and 
2 CONT Norway, however, remained united until 1814.
1 NOTE She was the youngest daughter of King Valdemar IV of Denmark. At the age of ten she was married to King Hσkon VI of Norway, son of Magnus II of Sweden and Norway. Their son Olaf, born in 1370, was elected King Olaf II of Denmark i
2 CONC n 1375 at the death of Margrethe's father, with her as regent. After her husband's death shortly after her son also became Olaf IV of Norway. After Olaf's death in 1387 the Estates in Denmark elected her as Full-mighty Husband and
2 CONC  Mistress for life. The following year she became regent of Norway. In 1388 the Swedish nobility dethroned their king Albrecht of Mecklenburg, and elected Margrethe as their reigning Queen instead. She chose her sister's daughter'
2 CONC s son Erik of Pommerania as her successor, who beacme king in 1389, but Margrethe remained the real ruler. She founded the union of Kalmer which in the case of Sweden would last until 1523, and with Norway until 1814. In 1410, Mar
2 CONC grethe tried to reinstate Danish overlordship over Schleswig, which caused a war with the Counts in Holstein. She traveled to the conflict area, and died there in 1412. She lived (1353-1412).
