1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00023863&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT      Marie von Mecklenburg, Duchess of Pomerania was born in 1363.1 She was the daughter of Heinrich I Herzog von Mecklenburg-Schwerin and Ingeborg Valdemarsdottir, Princess of Denmark.1 She married Wartislav VII of Pomerania , Du
2 CONC ke of Pomerania in 1380.1 She died circa 1402.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Marie von Mecklenburg, Duchess of Pomerania gained the title of Duchess of Pomerania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Marie von Mecklenburg, Duchess of Pomerania and Wartislav VII of Pomerania , Duke of Pomerania
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik VII of Pomerania, King of Denmark+1 b. 1382, d. c 1459
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine of Pomerania+1 b. 1390, d. 1426
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 17. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wartislaw VII, Duke of Pomerania
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Wartislaw VII of Pomerania)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wartislaw VII (Polish: Warcisław) (*1363/1365, † 1394/1395)[1] was one of the Dukes of Pomerania. He was the son of Bogislaw V, brother of Casimir IV and Bogislaw VIII. He married Maria of Mecklenburg and was the father of Eric of
2 CONC  Pomerania and Catherine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claims to Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT This country, the Hereditary Kingdom of Norway, has been the only medieval Scandinavian realm whose kingship was hereditary, not elective. Already when Olav IV of Norway was little and his mother Margaret was regent, the Dukes of 
2 CONC Mecklenburg advanced their claims.
2 CONT
2 CONT The right is based on their descent from Euphemia of Sweden, granddaughter of Haakon V of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Olav IV died in 1387, Norway was without a monarch, under the government of the regentess Margaret. She soon chose an heir, Eric of Pomerania, whose mother Maria of Mecklenburg had been Eufemia's eldest granddaughter. Maria's
2 CONC  uncle, Margaret's old opponent was left without.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Eric's nephew king Christopher died (before the death of the deposed Eric III of Norway), after some hiatus another magnate, Christian VIII of Oldenburg, of a female descent from Eufemia and the Mecklenburg (Eufemia's daughte
2 CONC r's great-grandson), was in 1450 chosen as king of Norway, this time surpassing his cousin and male-line rival, Duke Henry the Fat of Mecklenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Dukes of Mecklenburg continued to regard themselves as rightful heirs of Norway, however they were unable to gain the kingdom from the Oldenburgs.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Maria av Mecklenburg, född någon gång mellan 1363 och 1367, men troligen senast 1365, död efter 13 maj 1402, var en hertiginna av Pommern. Hon var dotter till hertig Henrik Bödeln av Mecklenburg (död 1383) och den danska prinsessa
2 CONC n Ingeborg Valdemarsdotter (död 1370), var hertiginna av Pommern.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon gifte sig 1380, före 23 mars, med hertig Vratislav VII av Pommern (stupad 1394 eller 1395) och fick med honom sonen Bogislav (född omkring 1382, död 1459), mer känd som den nordiske unionskungen Erik av Pommern, och dottern Ka
2 CONC tarina (född omkring 1390, död 1426), gift med pfalzgreve Johan av Pfalz (född omkring 1383, död 1443). Maria var även eventuell arvtagare till sin moster, den nordiska unionsdrottningen Margareta.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_av_Mecklenburg
