1 OCCU Riddare, riksråd, Riddare och riksråd, riddare, Riksråd, Nevnt 1290
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Ulf Holmgersson (Ama) till Rammshammar)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Holmger Folkesson (Ama) and Kristina Fastadotter 
2 CONT * Knight before 1276, Riksråd 1288 , died after 1290. Received on 13 February 1284 papal permission to marry his bride Elena, who is then said to be King Magnus "consanguinea" and therefore is probably identical with his sister Kr
2 CONC istina Birgersdotter's 1282 mentioned daughter with this name.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1) Ulf Holmgersson is mentioned no earlier than 1276 and is then called a knight. He is mentioned as a councilor in 1288 and still alive in 1290. He was first married to '''Cecilia Haraldsdotter,''' daughter of Harald 
2 CONC Gudmundsson ( winged lily ). They had four sons. 
2 CONT * Married: (2) on 1284 February 13, Ulf Holmgersson received a papal permit to marry his bride '''Helena Siggesdotter,''' with her he had three daughters and a son. (See Below SDHK No: 1266)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Cecilia Haraldsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''They had four sons'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Harald Ulfsson''' was 1293 kanik in Linköping. Owned land in Tjusts hd in Småland and died no later than 1305.
2 CONT * '''Holmger Ulfsson''' (d. Ä.) Or Holmger Ama, 1291-1307; married Ingegärd Unknown 
2 CONT * '''Charles Ulfsson''' only mentioned in 1305. Possibly this name is only a misspelling for Folke, since this does not appear in 1305 but on the other hand in 1307 when listing Ulf Holmgersson's sons.
2 CONT * '''Folke Ulfsson,''' Married  (1) Ingrid Larsdotter, (2) Sigrid Mårtensdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Helena Siggesdotter =
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christine/ Kristina ?,''' Born around 1285, a daughter married to Torkel Andersson (shared shield, later boat).  Her name li listed in her grandmother, Kristina Fastadotter Plant’s Will;  she states, And two silver flasks, on
2 CONC e another, her psaltery to little Kristina, if she survives the testator, of which Holmger's widow Helena from Sko should not have it instead - [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK%3A+762&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok
2 CONC =False&page=1&postid=sdhk_762&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab See, SDHK No: 762]
2 CONT * '''Lars Ulfsson (Ama)''' fl 1305-50; knight, councilor and lawyer in Södermanland Catherine. Entered 1323 in Vårfruberga monastery. Married (1) Ramborg Nilsdotter; married (2) Ingrid Anundsdotter
2 CONT * '''Holmger Ulfsson''' (dy), 1304—1311. Married Elena Sigmundsdotter (Båt)	 	 
2 CONT * '''Margrete''' married Leonard/Lidinvard/Lennart Ötheson, Iagman i Nárke
2 CONT * '''Katarina''' was in 1338 married to the knight Ulf Magnusson ( Lejonbalk ).
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ulf+Holmgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=13&postid=sdhk_1266&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 1266]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1284 February 13, of Issue: Orvieto'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pope Martin (IV) gives permission to grant an exemption for marriage between King M (agnus)'s relative Helena and Mr. Ulf Holmgersson, despite the fact that these are related in the fourth line, if it is true as claimed, that peac
2 CONC e in the kingdom between the king on the one hand side and mentioned Ulf and the other great men on the other are dependent on this marriage. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/1266.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ulf+Holmgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_1044&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 1044]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1278 January 2, of Issue: Ramshammar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Holmgersson and his wife C Haraldsdotter announce that Magnus Haraldsson of them has bought the farm Fivlered with all movable and immovable property for 180 marks money. The issuers seal - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?albu
2 CONC m_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000005432965467&photo_id=6000000143166573855&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ulf+Holmgersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_4146&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 4146]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1335 April 5'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Holmgersson, kanik in Uppsala and Västerås, bequeaths to Uppsala Cathedral's building, where he chooses to be buried, a farm in Helgestad, and to the improvement of the prebenda he held in Västerås 6 öresland in Ulsa and 1 öre
2 CONC sland in Vikby. He decides on numerous gifts in the form of money and other things, among other things. a. Strängnäs Cathedral, Linköping Cathedral, Vårfruberga Monastery, [https://www.geni.com/people/Kristina-Holmgersdotter-Ama/6
2 CONC 000000009702795258?through=6000000006820469588 Kristina Holmgersdotter], Alvastra Monastery, Nydala Monastery, Varnhems Monastery, Julita Monastery, the Preacher Brothers in Strängnäs, Sigtuna, Västerås, Skara, Lödöse, Skänninge, 
2 CONC Uppsala, Kalbr, Nöra Söderköping, Linköping, Jönköping, Skara, Arboga, Enköping, on to Sko kloster, Askeby kloster, S: ta Klara kloster in Stockholm, helgeandshuset in Uppsala, spetälskehuset in Enköping, hospital in Strängnäs, Sö
2 CONC derköping, Skänninge,
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus, Torkel Andersson, Birger Magnusson, and the issuer seal - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000001669618279?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000143167127867
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=12462 Hama Relatives]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By The Swedish Biographical Dictionary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 18 (1969-1971), page 73'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hama (Ama), branch of the Folkunga family (vol. 16) descended from Earl Birger's cousin Folke earl (d. 1210). His grandson the knight Ulf Holmgersson (lived 1290) was first gm a sister to the Södermanland lagmannen Anund Haraldsso
2 CONC n (Winged lily) and received in 1284 after her death papal exemption for marriage with a relative, a niece of Magnus ladulås. No later than 1288 he belonged to his council. Of his sons, Harald Ulfsson (d. Latest 1305) was kanik in
2 CONC  Linköping and the knight Holmger Ulfsson , also called Holmger H or Holmger Ama (d. 1307 or 1308), was King Birger's chamberlain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A third son Laurens Ulfsson(lived 1350) belonged to Duke Erik's followers in 1310 and became a knight around 1313. From 1318 he was in the Duchies Ingeborg's council, and no later than 1319 he became a lawyer in Södermanland after
2 CONC  King Birger's followers Stefan Röriksson (2 sparrows). At least from 1322 he belonged to King Magnus Eriksson's council. During his time as lawyer, a revision of the Södermann Act was approved in 1327. His manor was probably Ärnä
2 CONC s in Kärnbo (Söd), but he chose a burial ground in Alvastra monastery. The family carried in the weapon a shield cut from stone gables. It seems to have become extinct on the male side with Laurens Ulfsson's son Holmger Ama or Hol
2 CONC mger H (lived 1359) on Ärnäs. - 
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/11193 Lion Beam, Related]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By Swedish Biographical Dictionary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 22 (1977-1979), page 515'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lion bar, conventionally modern family name (first used in Laws of Judgment) for the descendants of non-family names on the mans side to the lawman of Tiohärad Karl Ingeborgsson (d earliest in 1266), who in his seal carried the sp
2 CONC lit shield with a lion in the heraldic right field o with the left field cut six times, so that it can be perceived as three beams. His wife was possibly the daughter of a half-sister on Birger Earl's ancestry, which should be com
2 CONC piled with the fact that his weapon may have been formed on the folk kid weapon. He was succeeded most recently in 1273 as a layman by his son the knight Folke Karlsson (d 1285 or 1286). 
2 CONT
2 CONT From about 1300 the same office was held by another son, the knight Magnus Karlsson(d at the earliest in 1316), which departed between 1304 and 1313, that is, several years before his death, probably as a result of Tiohärad's lega
2 CONC l case at the 1310 national division fell to King Birger. He can be besieged among Duke Eric's men already at his siege of Sthlm's castle 1306, was among his pledges in connection 1310 concerning morning gift and life gift to his 
2 CONC intended communion Sofia by Werle in the treaty of Helsingborg 1313 and so mentioned among the dukes' councils. Magnus Karlsson's first wife was the daughter of Birger Jarl's half-brother in the mother. In younger years he carried
2 CONC  in the seal the weapon with a wing which was then taken by his sister's husband the knight Ragvald Puke and his descendants, but from about 1305 he had the same weapon as his father. His son Ragvald Magnusson(d earliest in 1322) 
2 CONC occurs earliest among the great men, who in 1319 ratified the downturn between King Birger and his opponents, and was named governor in four letters from the years 1320 to 22. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Another son was Holmger Magnusson (d earliest in 1341), who in 1312 was about to travel to the Holy Land and by 1337 became a knight. He was the father of the Western Åskanik and kh in Hultsjö, Jönk, Magnus Holmgersson (d at the e
2 CONC arliest 1358), who at the beginning of the seal carried four-piece shield, probably his mother's weapon, but towards the end of his life, like the grandfather, the father's weapon resumed. His brother Ulf Holmgersson(d about 1396)
2 CONC  became a knight one of the years 1358–65 o sealed a letter in Västerås in connection with the negotiations there between the men of the peoples and king Albrekts in June 1365. In his Småland hometown he has not been able to occup
2 CONC y later than 1366. Next time Ulf Holmgersson shows up in the letter material is 1369 and 1370, when he appears at Akershus and Bohus among King Håkan's foremost men, and among these he is also mentioned in the standstill treaty wi
2 CONC th King Albrekts supporters at Edsviken in Sollentuna, Sth, 1371. In 1375 he sealed a letter in Tönsberg in Norway, o 1379 he is named among Håkan's councils and men. In 1386 Ulf Holmgersson exchanged land in Västergötland for lan
2 CONC d in Norway, and in 1388 he was one of the foremost among the Norwegian great men who in Oslo elected Håkan's widow Queen Margareta to Norway's mistress. The last times he appears are 1395, when he was among her many pledges from 
2 CONC the three Nordic kingdoms in the Lindholmen Treaty on King Albrekts release, etc. a few months later in Helsingborg, the letter dated her agreement with the Hanseates of Sthlm, Ulf Holmgersson was buried in Ids church in southeast
2 CONC ern Norway. That he did not return to Sweden after Margaret's victory should probably have explained that he married a daughter of King Magnus Eriksson's cousin, Norwegian great man Jon Hafthorsson (Roos).
2 CONT
