1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Helen of Sweden (c. 1190 – 1247, Swedish: Helena) was a Swedish princess and abbess, daughter of King Sverker II of Sweden and the mother of Queen Catherine of Sweden. She was Abbess of Vreta Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography	Edit Helen was born in Denmark, the daughter of King Sverker II and Queen Benecicta. Her father was an exile there at that time. In 1195 or 1196, he was crowned King of Sweden. In 1208, he was deposed, and in 1210, he di
2 CONC ed in battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen was the first of the three prominent victims of the Maid Abduction from Vreta, others being her daughter Benedicta of Bjelbo and granddaughter Ingrid Svantepolksdotter. Helen Sverkersdotter, the only daughter of the deposed 
2 CONC king, was educated at Vreta Abbey at the time of her father's death. Her relatives would not even hear the proposal of young Sune Folkason (died 1247), son of an earl who had been among Sverker's opponents in the battle in which h
2 CONC e himself fell. Sune Folkesson was of one of the two dynasties that been rivals for the Swedish throne since 1130, and Helen was from the other, the Sverker dynasty. Sune Folkason abducted Helena and took her, according to folklor
2 CONC e, to the Ymseborg Castle. They married, and two daughters survived from their marriage. Thus, the two Swedish dynasties were united, but only in a sideline.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1216, Helen's brother became King John I of Sweden. When he died childless in 1222, Helen and her daughters became heirs of the Sverker dynasty. One of her daughters, Catherine, in 1243 was married to King Eric XI, thus finally
2 CONC  uniting the two Swedish dynasties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Late in life, she is said to have become the Abbess of Vreta Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT References	Edit Lars O. Lagerqvist (1982). "Sverige och dess regenter under 1.000 år",("Sweden and its regents under a 1000 years") (in Swedish). Albert Bonniers Förlag AB. ISBN 91-0-075007-7. Borænius, Magnus i Klostret i Vreta i
2 CONC  Östergötland 1724 & 2003 s. 31
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/antiqtid/21/0438.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00275896&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ** http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena_Sverkersdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena Sverkersdotter, död 1247, var en svensk prinsessa och sedan abbedissa, dotter till kung Sverker den yngre och drottning Benedikta (Hvide).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon var enligt Magnus Boræn föreståndare i Vreta och gifte sig med jarlen Sune Folkesson efter att ha blivit bortrövad av honom från klostret 1210.
2 CONT
