1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Birgitta Arentsdotter Pinnow=
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 32254
2 CONT
2 CONT Utfärdat: 14890709, Uppsala Innehåll: Birgitta Arendsdotter (dotter till Arend Pinnow (björnhuvud)), änka efter herr Karl Magnusson (Eka-ätten), säljer med samtycke av sina arvingar till herr Erik Andree, prebendat i Stockholm och
2 CONC  kyrkoherde i Solna, sin tomt i Norrmalm utanför Stockholm för 60 mark reda penningar; tomten ska lyda under Helga fem unders (sårs) prebenda i Stockholms bykyrka.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Arendt Johansson Pinnow and Elin Andersdotter (Ulfstand av Årby)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eka%C3%A4tten '''Karl Magnusson (Eka)''']  Riddare, riksråd. Död 1467. Karl Magnusson (Eka) , knight and councilor. Married Birgitta Arendsdotter, daughter of Arend Pinnow and Elin Andersdot
2 CONC ter ( Årbyätten ).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Magnus Karlsson (Eka)'''. Riksråd, häradshövding. Död 1487 i Eka, Lillkyrka sn.
2 CONT *  '''Trotte Karlsson (Eka)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''' Sidan ändrades senast den 5 mars 2009 kl. 12.42.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birgitta_Arentsdotter_Pinnow Karl Magnusson (Eka Family)]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Magnusson (Eka family)
2 CONT Death:latest 1473
2 CONT
2 CONT Riksråd , Hövitsman , Riddare
2 CONT
2 CONT Band 12 (1949), page 574.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Merits'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Magnusson, the previous half-brother, was still alive on 21 Sept. 1467, was d 25 June 1473. Parents: the knight Magnus Trottesson and Märta Magnusdotter (Kase). Mentioned 29 June 1421, was district chief in Vaksala (Upps.) 17
2 CONC  June 1440 and still 28 Nov. 1457; knight apparently at the coronation of King Christopher 14 sept. 1441; was Riksråd 7 Oct. 1449; was a courtier on Kastelholm 18 March 1453 and 21 July 1463.
2 CONT
2 CONT G. m. Birgitta Arentsdotter (Pinnow), who was still alive 9 July 1489, daughter of the gunsmith Arent Pinnow and Elin Andersdotter (2 tips from above). .
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT K. wrote in 1447 and still in 1453 to his wife's farm Finsta but in the latter year bought Eka, which his brother Gregers previously owned, and then wrote to this farm. According to Ericus Olai , Karl Knutsson's
2 CONT
2 CONT Siege of Stockholm Castle in 1436 was attended by 300 of Archbishop Olof's men under the command of K. During the following period, he is often found at council meetings and lords' days. His political attitude has probably been in
2 CONC fluenced by his family ties with the Oxenstierna family - the brothers Bengt and Nils Jönsson were cousins ​​to his mother. At the settlement 10 Oct. 1441 between Karl Knutsson and Krister Nilsson (Vaasa), Bengt Jönsson's father-i
2 CONC n-law, K. was one of Krister's six promises and thus clearly appears as Karl Knutsson's opponent. After his accession to the throne, however, K. was used in his service. In the summer of 1449 he took part in the king's unfortunate
2 CONC  expedition to Gotland under Magnus Grens management. The same year he was present at the coronation in Trondheim. In 1453 he was called a courtier on Kastelholm and Åland. But when Karl Knutsson was expelled from the kingdom in 1
2 CONC 457 through Jöns Bengtsson's revolt, K. is again found among his opponents, and he was also one of the six gentlemen who in the so-called king's second defense statement were summoned to Danzig to be held accountable. During Krist
2 CONC ian I's time, K. appears in several letters as a member of the council aristocracy. In the summer of 1463, he accompanied the king on his journey to Finland and was then (July 21) again called courtier at Kastelholm. This castle w
2 CONC as 16 Oct. s. å. granted to Krister Bengtsson (Oxenstierna), who on this day had to make a solemn declaration to the king to keep it - the Oxenstierna group stood after the imprisonment of the archbishop, Jöns Bengtsson, in a tens
2 CONC e relationship with Kristian. As K. had only been a courtier at Kastelholm a few months earlier, the information about the granting of the castle to Krister is somewhat surprising, and its exact meaning is unknown. In the above-me
2 CONC ntioned declaration, however, K. appears as one of Krister's promises, which is another sign that he was close to the Oxenstiern group. When Jöns Bengtsson in the autumn of 1466 had to relinquish the governorship to Erik Axelsson 
2 CONC (Tott), who was supported by the council majority, K., however, stood on the latter's side judging by the settlement between the two parties; his son which is another sign that he was close to the Oxenstiern group. When Jöns Bengt
2 CONC sson in the autumn of 1466 had to relinquish the governorship to Erik Axelsson (Tott), who was supported by the council majority, who was supported by the council majority, K., however, stood on the latter's side judging by the se
2 CONC ttlement between the two parties; his son Trotte Karlsson (see below 4), on the other hand, was then one of Jöns' supporters. K. seems to have continued to have personal connections with him; the same winter, through a letter from
2 CONC  K., Jöns received some information about his enemies, Nils Sture's followers. When the development in 1467 led to Karl Knutsson's recall, K. was one of the councilors who issued the invitation to him to return. Then K. disappears
2 CONC  from the sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Corrections and additions made'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Refer to this article
2 CONT
2 CONT Of course, it is best if you can make a reference to the printed version. If you want to refer to the web version, you must make a link to the current page so that it is clear that it is the web version you are referring to. An ex
2 CONC ample of a reference to this article is: Karl Magnusson (Eka-släkt), https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/artikel/16783, Swedish biographical dictionary (species by Elsa Nordström.), Retrieved 2022-02- 14.
2 CONT
2 CONT You can also refer to this article using its unique URN number which is: urn: sbl: 16783 URN stands for Uniform Resource Name and is a logical identifier for this article, unlike its link, which is a physical identifier . This mea
2 CONC ns that a reference to the article's URN will always be valid, regardless of future changes to this website.
2 CONT
2 CONT Such a reference can look like this:
2 CONT Karl Magnusson (Eka family), urn: sbl: 16783, Swedish biographical dictionary (species by Elsa Nordström.), Retrieved 2022-02-14.
2 CONT
2 CONT Author
2 CONT Elsa Nordström.
